1
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,340
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:17,095 --> 00:00:20,265
(Taean)

3
00:00:20,805 --> 00:00:24,235
(Embracing the blue waters of the West Sea)

4
00:00:24,905 --> 00:00:28,575
(A place where vast tidal flats stretch out)

5
00:00:30,015 --> 00:00:32,815
(Sun-kissed salt fields...)

6
00:00:33,515 --> 00:00:38,115
(and bountiful farmlands stretch across the land.)

7
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:43,425
(Where there's an abundance of local produce)

8
00:00:44,155 --> 00:00:49,225
(Taean in South Chungcheong Province where nature's gifts are everywhere)

9
00:00:50,665 --> 00:00:55,165
(Today, a special festival is about to begin here.)

10
00:00:56,135 --> 00:00:58,735
(Who is the first to arrive?)

11
00:00:58,735 --> 00:00:59,805
One.

12
00:01:00,545 --> 00:01:01,945
Two, three, four.

13
00:01:03,315 --> 00:01:06,075
(Cho Jung Seok?)

14
00:01:06,075 --> 00:01:07,845
Five, six, seven, eight.

15
00:01:08,645 --> 00:01:10,385
(In a world of his own)

16
00:01:10,385 --> 00:01:11,385
(Turning)

17
00:01:11,385 --> 00:01:12,385
(Ta-da)

18
00:01:13,755 --> 00:01:15,855
(The dance initiation is complete.)

19
00:01:16,525 --> 00:01:18,825
(Cho Jung Seok arrives as a special guest in Taean.)

20
00:01:18,825 --> 00:01:19,825
Okay.

21
00:01:20,995 --> 00:01:23,795
(Jung Seok arrives 1 step ahead of the 4 siblings.)

22
00:01:24,095 --> 00:01:25,965
How do you know Jung Ah?

23
00:01:25,965 --> 00:01:27,505
- Well, I...
- What brings you here?

24
00:01:27,735 --> 00:01:28,865
First,

25
00:01:29,205 --> 00:01:31,775
we were in a movie called "Hit-and-Run Squad."

26
00:01:32,435 --> 00:01:35,775
When I was in "Hospital Playlist,"

27
00:01:35,775 --> 00:01:37,715
Sun Young made a special appearance.

28
00:01:38,145 --> 00:01:41,245
I don't have her number or anything,

29
00:01:41,715 --> 00:01:43,955
but somehow, I've had a strong sense...

30
00:01:43,955 --> 00:01:45,585
of familiarity with her.

31
00:01:46,455 --> 00:01:47,825
As for You Seok,

32
00:01:48,755 --> 00:01:50,155
I'll be meeting him for the first time today.

33
00:01:50,355 --> 00:01:52,795
He says that he wants to be like you.

34
00:01:52,795 --> 00:01:53,825
You're his role model.

35
00:01:53,965 --> 00:01:55,365
Really?

36
00:01:56,065 --> 00:01:57,895
He's a big fan of yours.

37
00:01:57,895 --> 00:01:58,935
Is that so?

38
00:01:59,395 --> 00:02:01,365
I'm very grateful.

39
00:02:02,105 --> 00:02:03,235
(How will You Seok react when he sees Jung Seok, his role model?)

40
00:02:03,235 --> 00:02:04,235
Is that right?

41
00:02:05,705 --> 00:02:08,405
- Shall we rehearse it?
- Sure, let's do it.

42
00:02:08,505 --> 00:02:09,545
How about...

43
00:02:09,545 --> 00:02:10,645
(Rehearsal?)

44
00:02:10,645 --> 00:02:11,675
While staying outside?

45
00:02:12,575 --> 00:02:13,715
They will be sitting here.

46
00:02:13,715 --> 00:02:16,915
(Did Jung Seok prepare a special event before coming to Taean?)

47
00:02:17,755 --> 00:02:20,225
(At that time, the four siblings...)

48
00:02:20,625 --> 00:02:22,625
- Hello.
- Hello.

49
00:02:23,755 --> 00:02:24,825
(Sun Young and You Seok are hand in hand.)

50
00:02:24,825 --> 00:02:25,895
- Sun Young.
- Yes?

51
00:02:25,895 --> 00:02:28,695
If we think about our work later, these aren't really mudflats.

52
00:02:29,295 --> 00:02:31,335
- What? The tide will go out soon.
- The tide is still in.

53
00:02:32,395 --> 00:02:35,605
(One person watching the scene unfold)

54
00:02:35,835 --> 00:02:37,305
They're holding each other's hand.

55
00:02:37,305 --> 00:02:38,335
(Watching them secretly while hiding)

56
00:02:38,775 --> 00:02:40,705
They look so sweet together.

57
00:02:42,045 --> 00:02:43,575
(Completely unaware of what's about to happen)

58
00:02:43,575 --> 00:02:44,815
- Hello.
- Hello.

59
00:02:45,945 --> 00:02:49,015
(Entering without suspecting anything)

60
00:02:49,585 --> 00:02:50,655
My goodness.

61
00:02:51,885 --> 00:02:54,085
It's beautiful. The view is amazing.

62
00:02:55,225 --> 00:02:58,455
(A spot with a perfect view of the sea)

63
00:02:58,955 --> 00:03:01,225
I seriously missed you so much.

64
00:03:02,365 --> 00:03:04,095
You Seok is very happy to be back.

65
00:03:04,095 --> 00:03:07,065
- I've been waiting for this.
- He says two nights are too short.

66
00:03:07,065 --> 00:03:08,635
Right after filming here, he wants to go to the next location...

67
00:03:08,635 --> 00:03:10,235
and continue filming.

68
00:03:10,435 --> 00:03:11,775
We should film for two whole weeks...

69
00:03:12,435 --> 00:03:14,075
until we get tired of seeing each other.

70
00:03:14,075 --> 00:03:16,075
You Seok loves being on this show.

71
00:03:16,375 --> 00:03:18,115
- What about you?
- I like it too.

72
00:03:18,515 --> 00:03:20,345
I love being on the show too.

73
00:03:20,615 --> 00:03:23,215
I want to spend 230 days with you all.

74
00:03:23,485 --> 00:03:26,285
(While the two siblings are in love with Fresh off the Sea)

75
00:03:26,955 --> 00:03:28,685
(Laughing)

76
00:03:29,025 --> 00:03:31,395
(Jung Ah and Yoon Seo come running with huge smiles.)

77
00:03:32,225 --> 00:03:35,195
(Completely happy)

78
00:03:35,295 --> 00:03:36,525
We should hurry to see them.

79
00:03:36,735 --> 00:03:38,565
- Isn't this place beautiful?
- My gosh.

80
00:03:38,565 --> 00:03:39,595
It's really beautiful.

81
00:03:42,105 --> 00:03:43,835
They're also holding hands.

82
00:03:44,375 --> 00:03:46,375
Everyone here is so affectionate.

83
00:03:47,575 --> 00:03:50,015
The older members are so warm...

84
00:03:50,615 --> 00:03:51,775
and full of love.

85
00:03:54,585 --> 00:03:55,585
Something smells delicious.

86
00:03:58,715 --> 00:04:00,485
Aren't they workers over there?

87
00:04:01,155 --> 00:04:02,625
- With them...
- Aren't they waiting for us?

88
00:04:03,125 --> 00:04:06,325
(Are they waiting to head out to sea with the four siblings?)

89
00:04:06,595 --> 00:04:07,965
We aren't getting abducted again, are we?

90
00:04:08,695 --> 00:04:10,295
- You think so?
- I'm worried.

91
00:04:11,735 --> 00:04:13,865
- Hello.
- Hello.

92
00:04:14,405 --> 00:04:16,465
Did you see those people waiting for us?

93
00:04:16,465 --> 00:04:18,505
- Where?
- Over there.

94
00:04:18,505 --> 00:04:20,205
These aren't mudflats.

95
00:04:20,205 --> 00:04:22,475
- Where are they?
- They're way over there.

96
00:04:22,745 --> 00:04:24,145
I saw about ten people waiting for us.

97
00:04:24,715 --> 00:04:26,985
- It must be a big boat.
- About ten people are waiting.

98
00:04:26,985 --> 00:04:28,145
- That's worrisome.
- I know.

99
00:04:28,715 --> 00:04:29,945
They're waiting for us, aren't they?

100
00:04:30,585 --> 00:04:31,715
- I don't know.
- No?

101
00:04:31,715 --> 00:04:34,085
- They always say they don't know.
- It's hard to believe them.

102
00:04:35,125 --> 00:04:37,425
Steamed clams, kimchi crab stew, cold raw fish soup,

103
00:04:37,425 --> 00:04:39,125
- and sea cucumber are recommended.
- Kimchi crab stew?

104
00:04:39,495 --> 00:04:40,795
- "Crab?" - Is it a stew made with crab?

105
00:04:40,795 --> 00:04:43,065
- Or clams?
- It must be a dish made with crab.

106
00:04:43,065 --> 00:04:44,135
(Gasping)

107
00:04:45,765 --> 00:04:46,765
It looks like shabu-shabu.

108
00:04:46,765 --> 00:04:47,835
(It's a hearty feast.)

109
00:04:48,405 --> 00:04:51,605
(To a refreshing, deeply flavorful broth,)

110
00:04:51,605 --> 00:04:54,745
(a whole octopus dives right in.)

111
00:04:57,375 --> 00:05:00,815
(A clear and refreshing octopus soup)

112
00:05:02,185 --> 00:05:03,215
(Jaw-dropping)

113
00:05:03,215 --> 00:05:04,415
Is it a crab?

114
00:05:04,755 --> 00:05:06,685
- There are clams.
- Abalone.

115
00:05:06,685 --> 00:05:07,825
It looks so good.

116
00:05:08,955 --> 00:05:10,395
- There are abalone and shrimp.
- Incredible.

117
00:05:12,295 --> 00:05:13,765
- It looks amazing.
- And squid.

118
00:05:13,765 --> 00:05:15,065
(Clams underneath abalone, shrimp, and squid)

119
00:05:15,665 --> 00:05:17,465
(Steamed clams, a generous harmony of seafood and clams)

120
00:05:19,535 --> 00:05:21,405
(Manila clam soup packed with clams from Taean)

121
00:05:21,505 --> 00:05:22,635
- That's a lot.
- It's cold raw fish soup.

122
00:05:22,635 --> 00:05:24,405
I love cold raw fish soup. The portion is generous.

123
00:05:24,905 --> 00:05:26,575
I've never seen it this beautifully presented before.

124
00:05:27,505 --> 00:05:28,945
- I love it. It's so beautiful.
- It looks very delicious.

125
00:05:29,405 --> 00:05:30,845
We're having such a healthy breakfast.

126
00:05:31,675 --> 00:05:32,875
(Exclaiming)

127
00:05:32,875 --> 00:05:34,645
- My gosh.
- Goodness.

128
00:05:34,645 --> 00:05:36,245
- I love noodles.
- Gosh.

129
00:05:36,515 --> 00:05:37,555
- The noodles.
- Goodness.

130
00:05:37,555 --> 00:05:38,855
(A bowl of noodles mixed into refreshing cold raw fish soup)

131
00:05:40,085 --> 00:05:41,225
I love this dish.

132
00:05:41,225 --> 00:05:44,355
(Slurping it down neatly)

133
00:05:44,995 --> 00:05:47,095
(One tangy, refreshing bite to wake up the appetite)

134
00:05:47,425 --> 00:05:48,465
Shall I try it?

135
00:05:48,465 --> 00:05:51,395
(Sun Young starts with steamed scallop.)

136
00:05:52,295 --> 00:05:53,635
(Her eyes light up.)

137
00:05:53,635 --> 00:05:54,635
Is it good?

138
00:05:54,835 --> 00:05:57,035
- Gosh, the scallop...
- We're a little...

139
00:05:57,605 --> 00:05:58,675
Abalone.

140
00:05:59,905 --> 00:06:01,905
(Tearing off the plump, chewy abalone)

141
00:06:02,005 --> 00:06:03,045
Is it good?

142
00:06:03,045 --> 00:06:05,115
(Taking a huge bite)

143
00:06:05,575 --> 00:06:06,645
It's good.

144
00:06:08,985 --> 00:06:11,415
(I'll try some octopus soup too.)

145
00:06:12,055 --> 00:06:13,725
(Scooping up a generous serving)

146
00:06:13,725 --> 00:06:14,785
Thank you.

147
00:06:14,785 --> 00:06:16,755
(Passing it to the youngest)

148
00:06:17,125 --> 00:06:18,495
(It looks delicious.)

149
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:21,625
(Yoon Seo slurps up the broth.)

150
00:06:21,625 --> 00:06:22,665
It's good.

151
00:06:22,665 --> 00:06:23,965
(Yoon Seo slurps up the broth.)

152
00:06:25,165 --> 00:06:27,165
(You Seok digs into the clam meat.)

153
00:06:27,165 --> 00:06:28,235
It's a razor shell.

154
00:06:28,235 --> 00:06:29,305
- A razor shell?
- Yes.

155
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,975
(You Seok digs into the clam meat.)

156
00:06:31,805 --> 00:06:35,945
(Packed with the taste of the sea, how is the Manila clam soup?)

157
00:06:37,315 --> 00:06:39,975
(Going straight for the chewy Manila clam)

158
00:06:40,415 --> 00:06:41,485
(This is the taste.)

159
00:06:42,245 --> 00:06:44,215
(Chuckling)

160
00:06:44,215 --> 00:06:45,285
What's the matter?

161
00:06:45,915 --> 00:06:47,385
- We'll probably catch one of these.
- Right.

162
00:06:47,385 --> 00:06:49,725
- Which one will it be?
- Let's be relaxed when we eat.

163
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:53,695
(The creatures they might be catching today)

164
00:06:54,295 --> 00:06:55,595
What's in season right now?

165
00:06:56,595 --> 00:06:57,895
Clams and...

166
00:06:58,965 --> 00:07:00,365
(It's a mystery.)

167
00:07:00,565 --> 00:07:02,005
There's only one squid, so it can't be that.

168
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:03,035
(There's only one squid, so it can't be that.)

169
00:07:03,505 --> 00:07:04,535
(Her guess is surprisingly well founded.)

170
00:07:04,535 --> 00:07:06,205
If it's squid, there should be a lot of squid.

171
00:07:07,075 --> 00:07:09,375
I don't care. Whatever it is, I'm going.

172
00:07:09,945 --> 00:07:11,345
- We can handle it anyway.
- Right.

173
00:07:11,975 --> 00:07:12,975
Of course.

174
00:07:12,975 --> 00:07:16,515
After everything we went through last time...

175
00:07:16,515 --> 00:07:17,685
(They're completely absorbed in guessing their work.)

176
00:07:18,815 --> 00:07:20,085
(Meanwhile, Jung Seok makes his move.)

177
00:07:20,085 --> 00:07:22,525
As a secret guest, I'm nervous.

178
00:07:22,785 --> 00:07:25,125
I hope the hosts will be happy to see me.

179
00:07:25,725 --> 00:07:27,295
(Sneaking off before anyone notices)

180
00:07:28,025 --> 00:07:30,635
(Finally, he's right around the corner.)

181
00:07:31,265 --> 00:07:33,565
(Warming up for one last time)

182
00:07:34,035 --> 00:07:36,065
- We must be catching octopus.
- Octopus?

183
00:07:36,935 --> 00:07:38,005
Octopus.

184
00:07:38,005 --> 00:07:39,475
(The speculation about today's catch continues.)

185
00:07:40,305 --> 00:07:43,045
As you know, we're in Taean now.

186
00:07:43,045 --> 00:07:44,115
- Right.
- Right.

187
00:07:44,715 --> 00:07:46,715
- Today, you're heading...
- Yes.

188
00:07:46,715 --> 00:07:49,645
to a rock festival...

189
00:07:49,645 --> 00:07:52,155
- being held in Taean.
- What?

190
00:07:52,155 --> 00:07:53,825
Gosh, that's awesome.

191
00:07:54,725 --> 00:07:56,025
A rock festival?

192
00:07:56,185 --> 00:07:57,255
(Bouncing her feet with excitement)

193
00:07:57,255 --> 00:07:58,725
Why?

194
00:07:59,525 --> 00:08:02,125
- Do you mean rock music?
- Why all of a sudden?

195
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:03,595
(Rock music in Taean?)

196
00:08:03,595 --> 00:08:05,335
Why all of a sudden? This is awesome.

197
00:08:05,335 --> 00:08:07,235
- A rock festival?
- We're going to a festival?

198
00:08:07,235 --> 00:08:10,275
- Can we watch the concerts?
- But it seems quiet here.

199
00:08:10,275 --> 00:08:11,305
You're lying.

200
00:08:11,405 --> 00:08:13,135
- How are they lying?
- You'll let us watch the concerts?

201
00:08:13,135 --> 00:08:14,345
We'll give you a hint.

202
00:08:14,345 --> 00:08:15,775
My gosh. What is it?

203
00:08:15,775 --> 00:08:16,845
Please give them a hint.

204
00:08:17,445 --> 00:08:19,015
By "rock,"

205
00:08:19,015 --> 00:08:20,915
- A rock?
- they must mean an actual rock.

206
00:08:21,685 --> 00:08:23,755
- A rock?
- A rock?

207
00:08:24,455 --> 00:08:25,715
(Suddenly, a red carpet appears.)

208
00:08:25,855 --> 00:08:27,385
What's this? It's a red carpet.

209
00:08:27,385 --> 00:08:29,455
(A mysterious red carpet spreads out.)

210
00:08:30,085 --> 00:08:31,125
What's going on?

211
00:08:31,955 --> 00:08:33,025
I hear music.

212
00:08:34,125 --> 00:08:35,165
What is it?

213
00:08:36,065 --> 00:08:37,395
Do we have a guest today?

214
00:08:38,365 --> 00:08:40,365
- Seriously?
- We must have a guest today.

215
00:08:40,365 --> 00:08:42,705
- We have a guest on the first day?
- Really?

216
00:08:43,465 --> 00:08:44,535
Is it a rocker?

217
00:08:45,375 --> 00:08:48,445
- This is amazing. What is it?
- Please come in.

218
00:08:49,605 --> 00:08:52,675
(The song sounds familiar.)

219
00:08:53,215 --> 00:08:54,385
Is Lee Jae Hoon coming?

220
00:08:54,385 --> 00:08:55,545
Isn't it Cho Jung Seok?

221
00:08:55,885 --> 00:08:58,215
I think it's Cho Jung Seok. Isn't it him?

222
00:08:58,215 --> 00:08:59,285
Isn't it Cho Jung Seok?

223
00:08:59,285 --> 00:09:02,325
- I think so. Jung Seok...
- I'm his huge fan.

224
00:09:03,025 --> 00:09:04,095
Jung Seok?

225
00:09:04,095 --> 00:09:06,095
(Could it be Cho Jung Seok, my role model?)

226
00:09:06,355 --> 00:09:07,425
(Full of anticipation)

227
00:09:07,425 --> 00:09:08,425
Really?

228
00:09:09,125 --> 00:09:10,125
Is Cho Jung Seok coming?

229
00:09:10,125 --> 00:09:11,435
(Really? Cho Jung Seok?)

230
00:09:11,765 --> 00:09:14,065
(No way...)

231
00:09:15,435 --> 00:09:17,735
There's only thing I hope for

232
00:09:18,835 --> 00:09:21,175
(A guest artist at the rock festival, Cho Jung Seok)

233
00:09:21,745 --> 00:09:24,115
(Screaming)

234
00:09:26,915 --> 00:09:30,885
(Screaming)

235
00:09:32,015 --> 00:09:34,255
(Hopping with excitement)

236
00:09:34,685 --> 00:09:36,785
(How about You Seok whose role model is Jung Seok?)

237
00:09:36,785 --> 00:09:38,495
This is awesome!

238
00:09:40,225 --> 00:09:42,325
Seriously?

239
00:09:42,695 --> 00:09:43,695
(Blurred)

240
00:09:43,695 --> 00:09:45,035
(He's so surprised that he forgot to swallow.)

241
00:09:45,235 --> 00:09:46,435
My goodness.

242
00:09:46,435 --> 00:09:47,665
- Jung Seok.
- Hello.

243
00:09:47,665 --> 00:09:50,305
- Jung Seok.
- I can't believe this.

244
00:09:50,305 --> 00:09:51,505
(Are we dreaming?)

245
00:09:52,935 --> 00:09:55,205
- Gosh.
- Nice to meet you.

246
00:09:55,205 --> 00:09:56,245
(He also says hello to You Seok.)

247
00:09:56,245 --> 00:09:57,275
This is awesome.

248
00:09:57,845 --> 00:10:01,615
(Swept up in the warm welcome,)

249
00:10:01,985 --> 00:10:06,815
(he finally gets to sing a little something.)

250
00:10:06,985 --> 00:10:11,125
So it never loses its light

251
00:10:12,195 --> 00:10:16,025
(The guest artist rolls up the red carpet himself.)

252
00:10:16,325 --> 00:10:17,395
I'll stop here.

253
00:10:18,295 --> 00:10:19,365
This is insane.

254
00:10:19,365 --> 00:10:20,405
(Cho Jung Seok's surprise entrance is a huge success.)

255
00:10:20,405 --> 00:10:22,735
- It's nice to meet you all.
- This is wonderful.

256
00:10:22,935 --> 00:10:24,375
- Gosh.
- It's lovely to see you.

257
00:10:24,375 --> 00:10:25,775
- It must be a rock festival...
- This is insane.

258
00:10:25,775 --> 00:10:27,145
because of "Seok" in his name.

259
00:10:27,505 --> 00:10:30,775
Last night, we couldn't stop talking...

260
00:10:30,775 --> 00:10:33,315
- about who the guest would be.
- Seriously.

261
00:10:33,315 --> 00:10:35,585
- I didn't imagine this at all.
- I'm so happy.

262
00:10:35,945 --> 00:10:38,855
- I've been wanting to see you.
- I know, Yoon Seo.

263
00:10:39,455 --> 00:10:40,585
This is amazing.

264
00:10:40,585 --> 00:10:42,855
- I can't believe you're here.
- It's Cho Jung Seok.

265
00:10:42,855 --> 00:10:43,995
Believe it or not, I'm here.

266
00:10:43,995 --> 00:10:44,995
(They met once on Jung Seok's online channel.)

267
00:10:45,595 --> 00:10:47,695
(Thank you for coming.)

268
00:10:47,865 --> 00:10:49,825
This is unbelievable.

269
00:10:49,825 --> 00:10:50,935
(Welcome)

270
00:10:51,195 --> 00:10:52,795
This is so much fun.

271
00:10:52,795 --> 00:10:55,605
- Seriously.
- We have a guest on our first day.

272
00:10:55,865 --> 00:10:57,535
Thank you for welcoming me.

273
00:10:57,535 --> 00:10:59,875
I'm so happy to see you, Jung Seok.

274
00:10:59,875 --> 00:11:02,375
My plan was to sing while walking towards here.

275
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:06,315
I was going to sing here and say hello,

276
00:11:06,315 --> 00:11:08,745
- but my plan went out the window.
- We ran towards you.

277
00:11:08,745 --> 00:11:09,745
We got too excited.

278
00:11:10,485 --> 00:11:13,255
(She was just so happy to see him.)

279
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:16,225
- We were so happy to see you.
- Thank you so much.

280
00:11:16,225 --> 00:11:17,495
(Thank you for an enthusiastic welcome.)

281
00:11:18,325 --> 00:11:20,625
I never imagined seeing Jung Seok in Taean.

282
00:11:21,425 --> 00:11:23,625
- Please speak casually with me.
- What?

283
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:26,265
- Seriously, speak casually with me.
- Okay, Jung Seok.

284
00:11:27,305 --> 00:11:30,205
I'm so excited. He's one of my favorite actors.

285
00:11:30,435 --> 00:11:32,535
I've always felt a personal connection with you.

286
00:11:32,535 --> 00:11:34,305
I'm your huge fan.

287
00:11:34,705 --> 00:11:37,215
- I really like you too.
- Thank you.

288
00:11:37,215 --> 00:11:39,545
- I also like you so much.
- I like you a lot.

289
00:11:39,645 --> 00:11:41,515
- I like you even more.
- You're my favorite.

290
00:11:41,515 --> 00:11:43,045
- No, I like you more.
- I like you more.

291
00:11:43,045 --> 00:11:44,755
No, I like you even more.

292
00:11:45,755 --> 00:11:47,285
(What's going on here?)

293
00:11:48,055 --> 00:11:51,495
(You Seok just smiles without saying a word.)

294
00:11:51,925 --> 00:11:53,255
(This is awesome!)

295
00:11:53,525 --> 00:11:55,265
(Seriously?)

296
00:11:56,125 --> 00:11:59,165
(His overwhelming admiration leaves him briefly speechless.)

297
00:11:59,535 --> 00:12:02,705
(Just looking at him is enough.)

298
00:12:02,835 --> 00:12:04,435
- Someone who looks like you...
- Why are you just smiling?

299
00:12:04,435 --> 00:12:06,075
Me? Gosh.

300
00:12:06,075 --> 00:12:07,345
I don't know what to say.

301
00:12:07,545 --> 00:12:10,045
- Just looking at Jung Seok...
- I can't think straight.

302
00:12:10,275 --> 00:12:12,645
I can't even think straight.

303
00:12:13,245 --> 00:12:15,445
- Jung Seok...
- He's just so happy...

304
00:12:15,445 --> 00:12:16,545
just to look at you.

305
00:12:16,545 --> 00:12:18,055
- I feel like...
- With his role model...

306
00:12:18,055 --> 00:12:20,555
- My heart is fluttering so much.
- Of course. I'd feel the same.

307
00:12:20,555 --> 00:12:22,525
You Seok, please relax. I'll be casual with you too.

308
00:12:22,525 --> 00:12:23,795
- Please do.
- Yes.

309
00:12:24,025 --> 00:12:25,455
He's my number one...

310
00:12:25,455 --> 00:12:27,795
- You love him very much.
- Whenever...

311
00:12:27,795 --> 00:12:28,825
I'm not just saying this.

312
00:12:29,325 --> 00:12:31,895
Whenever I'm being interviewed...

313
00:12:31,895 --> 00:12:32,895
(A heartfelt confession from a true fan)

314
00:12:32,895 --> 00:12:34,835
I always say that you're my role model.

315
00:12:34,835 --> 00:12:36,965
I feel very grateful.

316
00:12:36,965 --> 00:12:39,335
You'll be sleeping next to your role model tonight.

317
00:12:39,335 --> 00:12:41,705
- You must be so excited.
- I won't be able to sleep tonight.

318
00:12:41,705 --> 00:12:43,205
- I won't be able to sleep.
- My goodness.

319
00:12:43,205 --> 00:12:44,875
- I envy you.
- I won't be able to sleep.

320
00:12:44,875 --> 00:12:45,915
I feel nervous too.

321
00:12:46,645 --> 00:12:48,245
Seriously.

322
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:51,315
(You Seok is blushing.)

323
00:12:51,315 --> 00:12:53,085
- You must feel very shy.
- Yes, I do.

324
00:12:53,085 --> 00:12:54,385
- What's the matter with him?
- What do we do?

325
00:12:54,385 --> 00:12:57,655
I would never feel like this for any other guest.

326
00:12:57,655 --> 00:12:59,195
(He's happy like he has the whole world.)

327
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:01,165
All right, hold my hand.

328
00:13:01,995 --> 00:13:03,325
What is it about me that you like so much?

329
00:13:04,965 --> 00:13:06,095
Things like this.

330
00:13:07,405 --> 00:13:10,205
- His ears turned red.
- I know. He's on cloud nine.

331
00:13:10,205 --> 00:13:11,835
- Gosh, thank you.
- My goodness.

332
00:13:11,835 --> 00:13:13,205
(Jung Seok is touched by You Seok's genuine confession.)

333
00:13:13,205 --> 00:13:14,705
- That must be nice.
- I don't know how to act.

334
00:13:14,705 --> 00:13:15,705
Right.

335
00:13:15,805 --> 00:13:17,045
I'm really curious.

336
00:13:17,045 --> 00:13:21,015
Both Jung Seok and Gummy are incredible singers. Do they...

337
00:13:21,015 --> 00:13:22,885
even go to karaoke together?

338
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,815
We used to go to karaoke a lot when we were dating.

339
00:13:24,815 --> 00:13:26,015
- I see.
- Did you sing together?

340
00:13:26,015 --> 00:13:27,015
The two of us.

341
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:28,325
You should've invited me.

342
00:13:29,285 --> 00:13:30,795
I would've loved to listen to you sing.

343
00:13:30,795 --> 00:13:33,055
- We can stay in the next room.
- Exactly.

344
00:13:33,195 --> 00:13:34,265
- I want to hear them sing.
- Just listening to them...

345
00:13:34,265 --> 00:13:36,495
We have a microphone at home with speakers.

346
00:13:36,495 --> 00:13:39,135
- That's very good.
- We use that to sing together.

347
00:13:39,165 --> 00:13:40,335
We really enjoy that.

348
00:13:40,495 --> 00:13:42,265
It must be nice to sing with Gummy.

349
00:13:42,605 --> 00:13:43,705
Right.

350
00:13:43,705 --> 00:13:46,405
Watching them made me dream about getting married.

351
00:13:46,405 --> 00:13:47,405
(Seeing Jung Seok and Gummy makes her want to get married.)

352
00:13:47,405 --> 00:13:48,675
I only saw...

353
00:13:48,675 --> 00:13:49,945
- the beautiful side of it.
- Right.

354
00:13:50,105 --> 00:13:51,445
Married life isn't always like that.

355
00:13:52,645 --> 00:13:54,915
- You've only seen that side.
- It's just one side.

356
00:13:54,915 --> 00:13:56,115
(Laughing)

357
00:13:56,185 --> 00:13:57,755
Jung Seok must feel hot.

358
00:13:57,815 --> 00:13:59,155
No, I'm fine.

359
00:13:59,155 --> 00:14:00,885
It's because I'm in the spotlight.

360
00:14:00,885 --> 00:14:02,625
(Fanning him with their hands)

361
00:14:02,625 --> 00:14:03,655
- I'm kidding.
- Oh, no.

362
00:14:03,655 --> 00:14:05,325
Actually, it's nice and cool.

363
00:14:05,325 --> 00:14:06,995
- It's because I'm eating hot food.
- Right.

364
00:14:07,395 --> 00:14:09,425
(Peeling a shrimp quietly)

365
00:14:09,495 --> 00:14:10,765
(Sending it straight to Jung Seok's plate)

366
00:14:10,765 --> 00:14:12,095
- Counterfeit money...
- I see.

367
00:14:12,865 --> 00:14:13,865
And so...

368
00:14:15,705 --> 00:14:17,375
- What?
- I peeled one for you.

369
00:14:17,805 --> 00:14:19,275
I was about to peel you one.

370
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:20,305
My goodness.

371
00:14:20,305 --> 00:14:21,445
What are they doing?

372
00:14:21,575 --> 00:14:23,945
- I saw You Seok peeling one, - Really?

373
00:14:23,945 --> 00:14:26,475
so I wanted to peel 1 for him. Then I found 1 on my plate.

374
00:14:26,945 --> 00:14:27,985
He's so thoughtful.

375
00:14:28,745 --> 00:14:29,785
Thank you.

376
00:14:29,985 --> 00:14:31,555
(Love is blossoming at the table.)

377
00:14:32,515 --> 00:14:33,815
You Seok, say something.

378
00:14:34,455 --> 00:14:37,655
I can't get any words out. What do I do?

379
00:14:37,895 --> 00:14:39,095
(Jung Seok also peels a shrimp carefully.)

380
00:14:39,095 --> 00:14:41,965
- You have to eat this part.
- Okay.

381
00:14:41,965 --> 00:14:43,425
It's the best part of the shrimp.

382
00:14:44,195 --> 00:14:47,335
(Enjoying the precious shrimp peeled by his senior)

383
00:14:47,335 --> 00:14:49,005
I feel so good today.

384
00:14:49,735 --> 00:14:51,035
I will work hard.

385
00:14:51,105 --> 00:14:52,835
Let's work hard and earn a lot of money.

386
00:14:52,835 --> 00:14:54,445
We should make him something delicious.

387
00:14:55,545 --> 00:14:56,975
I'll also work hard.

388
00:14:57,445 --> 00:14:58,545
(The four siblings promise to work hard.)

389
00:14:58,545 --> 00:14:59,745
Anyway, you're here...

390
00:14:59,745 --> 00:15:02,585
as a guest singer for today's rock festival.

391
00:15:02,585 --> 00:15:03,645
(That's so funny.)

392
00:15:03,645 --> 00:15:04,815
I only sang one verse.

393
00:15:05,985 --> 00:15:07,115
(Laughing)

394
00:15:07,115 --> 00:15:08,385
- One verse...
- It's time to go...

395
00:15:08,385 --> 00:15:09,625
to the rock festival.

396
00:15:09,625 --> 00:15:10,825
- Really?
- Seriously?

397
00:15:10,825 --> 00:15:12,525
Weren't you just saying that because Jung Seok was coming?

398
00:15:12,755 --> 00:15:14,765
- Is there a real rock festival...
- Really?

399
00:15:14,765 --> 00:15:15,765
in Taean?

400
00:15:15,765 --> 00:15:17,095
I didn't bring any outfit.

401
00:15:17,095 --> 00:15:19,835
We need to dress up for a rock festival.

402
00:15:20,465 --> 00:15:22,005
I thought that you meant the guest.

403
00:15:22,005 --> 00:15:23,905
We must be catching crabs off the rocks.

404
00:15:23,905 --> 00:15:24,975
- Right.
- Off the rocks.

405
00:15:24,975 --> 00:15:26,335
- We're doing something on rocks.
- That's what "rock" meant.

406
00:15:26,335 --> 00:15:28,005
They meant those rocks.

407
00:15:28,005 --> 00:15:30,075
We wouldn't go to a real rock festival, would we?

408
00:15:30,075 --> 00:15:32,815
(What exactly is this mysterious rock festival?)

409
00:15:33,245 --> 00:15:35,145
- Shall we get going now?
- Let's go.

410
00:15:35,145 --> 00:15:36,215
- Jung Seok.
- Yes?

411
00:15:36,215 --> 00:15:37,855
- Let's go.
- Yes, let's get going.

412
00:15:37,855 --> 00:15:38,955
(Just looking at him makes her smile.)

413
00:15:38,955 --> 00:15:40,585
What exciting adventures...

414
00:15:40,585 --> 00:15:42,625
(What exciting adventures await them?)

415
00:15:42,725 --> 00:15:44,395
It's definitely a rock festival.

416
00:15:44,395 --> 00:15:46,455
- Stop lying.
- If it's "rock,"

417
00:15:46,455 --> 00:15:47,825
there will be crabs.

418
00:15:47,825 --> 00:15:49,965
- We must be catching crabs.
- Crabs live between rocks.

419
00:15:50,365 --> 00:15:52,665
- Crabs are also in season.
- We're definitely catching crabs.

420
00:15:53,065 --> 00:15:54,465
I'll drive.

421
00:15:54,465 --> 00:15:55,805
- Really?
- Yes.

422
00:15:55,805 --> 00:15:56,865
You Seok, get in the front.

423
00:15:57,835 --> 00:15:58,935
My goodness.

424
00:15:58,935 --> 00:16:00,475
(You Seok claims the seat next to Jung Seok.)

425
00:16:00,475 --> 00:16:02,305
Can you play that? I want to hear it again.

426
00:16:02,575 --> 00:16:04,215
(Jung Seok recently released a new song.)

427
00:16:04,345 --> 00:16:05,945
You don't have to play it.

428
00:16:05,945 --> 00:16:07,415
But I want to hear it.

429
00:16:07,415 --> 00:16:08,885
(Yoon Seo's first song pick of the day)

430
00:16:09,315 --> 00:16:12,985
("You Changed My World" by Jung Seok)

431
00:16:13,515 --> 00:16:15,925
I'm actually riding in the car Jung Seok is driving.

432
00:16:17,185 --> 00:16:18,225
(Giggling)

433
00:16:18,225 --> 00:16:20,095
- I'll take good care of you.
- Jung Seok is driving us.

434
00:16:20,095 --> 00:16:22,165
(Riding in a car driven by their ultimate favorite)

435
00:16:22,165 --> 00:16:23,965
- I'll learn this song quickly.
- Right.

436
00:16:23,965 --> 00:16:25,665
(Listening to their favorite artist's song on the way)

437
00:16:27,405 --> 00:16:29,665
(Naturally grabbing the handheld microphone)

438
00:16:30,305 --> 00:16:31,975
(It's only you)

439
00:16:31,975 --> 00:16:34,505
(Humming along with all her heart)

440
00:16:34,505 --> 00:16:40,515
(My one and only love in this world)

441
00:16:40,515 --> 00:16:41,585
(Frowning)

442
00:16:41,845 --> 00:16:43,015
(I love you)

443
00:16:43,015 --> 00:16:44,285
Yoon Seo already memorized the lyrics.

444
00:16:44,285 --> 00:16:45,285
(She can't resist humming along even while getting ready.)

445
00:16:45,285 --> 00:16:46,355
What's the title of the song?

446
00:16:46,355 --> 00:16:49,285
"You Changed My World."

447
00:16:49,285 --> 00:16:50,795
Yoon Seo, you really memorized it.

448
00:16:50,795 --> 00:16:52,295
(Exclaiming proudly)

449
00:16:52,295 --> 00:16:55,525
- "You Changed..." - "You Changed..."

450
00:16:55,525 --> 00:16:57,495
- "My World." - "My World."

451
00:16:57,795 --> 00:16:59,335
(They finished studying Jung Seok's new song.)

452
00:16:59,795 --> 00:17:01,605
(Meanwhile, the fan quietly sitting in the front seat)

453
00:17:01,605 --> 00:17:03,635
- Do you like driving?
- No.

454
00:17:04,175 --> 00:17:05,375
(The conversation ends.)

455
00:17:05,375 --> 00:17:06,935
Just like you, I don't like it either.

456
00:17:06,935 --> 00:17:08,775
Would you let someone drive?

457
00:17:08,775 --> 00:17:09,775
It's like one of those things.

458
00:17:09,775 --> 00:17:12,445
I have to be the one grilling the meat.

459
00:17:12,445 --> 00:17:14,445
- You know what I mean?
- Yes.

460
00:17:14,445 --> 00:17:16,745
I feel like I have to be the one driving.

461
00:17:16,745 --> 00:17:17,755
(One man malfunctioning next to his role model)

462
00:17:17,755 --> 00:17:18,815
I feel somewhat obligated.

463
00:17:19,355 --> 00:17:21,925
(Once again, the conversation ends.)

464
00:17:21,925 --> 00:17:24,695
I saw a Pirate Ship over here yesterday.

465
00:17:24,795 --> 00:17:25,795
(Changing the subject)

466
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:27,925
- A Pirate Ship?
- Did you want to ride that too?

467
00:17:27,925 --> 00:17:28,925
Is that so?

468
00:17:28,925 --> 00:17:30,565
There's a small Pirate Ship.

469
00:17:30,565 --> 00:17:31,835
Is that so?

470
00:17:31,835 --> 00:17:33,165
(Embarrassed)

471
00:17:33,165 --> 00:17:36,835
(You Seok gets flustered several times today.)

472
00:17:36,835 --> 00:17:39,335
Last time, we did everything that he wanted to do.

473
00:17:39,335 --> 00:17:41,505
We rode the luge and went on a boat.

474
00:17:41,975 --> 00:17:43,105
- Is that so?
- Yes.

475
00:17:43,105 --> 00:17:44,215
That must've been nice.

476
00:17:44,215 --> 00:17:47,075
Jung Ah and Sun Young said, "Do you really have to do that?"

477
00:17:47,375 --> 00:17:49,715
Anyway, everything ended up being fun.

478
00:17:49,815 --> 00:17:50,855
It was so much fun.

479
00:17:51,915 --> 00:17:55,955
You Seok, did you check the destination?

480
00:17:56,485 --> 00:17:58,525
(Speaking of which,)

481
00:17:58,525 --> 00:18:01,765
(what could be this rock festival?)

482
00:18:02,065 --> 00:18:05,435
(You Seok looks up the destination on GPS.)

483
00:18:05,435 --> 00:18:07,705
- It's in front of the sea.
- It's in front of the sea?

484
00:18:07,705 --> 00:18:09,635
I'm sure it's the mudflats.

485
00:18:10,205 --> 00:18:14,545
Earlier, I saw a sign for a tidal flat experience center.

486
00:18:15,245 --> 00:18:18,445
(A sign for a tidal flat experience center catches You Seok's eye.)

487
00:18:18,545 --> 00:18:21,245
Tidal flat experience centers are the best.

488
00:18:21,545 --> 00:18:23,385
- It won't be an experience for us.
- We have to make money.

489
00:18:23,385 --> 00:18:25,715
- This is survival.
- It's our livelihood.

490
00:18:25,715 --> 00:18:27,685
We need to earn enough to pay for dinner tonight.

491
00:18:27,685 --> 00:18:28,685
- Yes.
- Right.

492
00:18:28,685 --> 00:18:29,725
(Everyone is convinced that they're going to work.)

493
00:18:29,725 --> 00:18:32,355
We must make a lot of money to treat Jung Seok.

494
00:18:32,355 --> 00:18:33,595
We'll make him delicious food.

495
00:18:33,595 --> 00:18:34,865
- I want to buy him beef.
- It's okay.

496
00:18:35,095 --> 00:18:36,695
(Gasping)

497
00:18:36,695 --> 00:18:37,695
(This whole place is a mudflat.)

498
00:18:37,695 --> 00:18:40,035
- This whole place is a mudflat.
- It's a mudflat.

499
00:18:40,035 --> 00:18:41,135
(Is it a real mudflat in front of them?)

500
00:18:41,135 --> 00:18:42,235
Look over there.

501
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:48,245
(Stretching out before the siblings)

502
00:18:49,675 --> 00:18:51,475
(With no end in sight)

503
00:18:51,475 --> 00:18:54,815
(A vast, endless tidal flat)

504
00:18:57,145 --> 00:18:59,415
(A massive stage to match the siblings' scale)

505
00:19:00,785 --> 00:19:03,655
(Guests start pour in after hearing about the festival.)

506
00:19:03,785 --> 00:19:06,255
(The front row at the rock festival is mine.)

507
00:19:07,495 --> 00:19:09,825
- We're going into the mudflat.
- This is my first time.

508
00:19:09,825 --> 00:19:11,095
(At last, they arrive at today's festival venue.)

509
00:19:11,565 --> 00:19:14,405
(In front of a fishing co-op building?)

510
00:19:15,505 --> 00:19:16,805
Is there another surprise?

511
00:19:16,865 --> 00:19:17,975
Look over there.

512
00:19:18,905 --> 00:19:20,705
(Surrounded by...)

513
00:19:20,705 --> 00:19:24,945
(all sorts of mysterious equipment with no clear purpose...)

514
