- Yes, I have.

1010
00:39:00,415 --> 00:39:01,985
(Her speed impresses the original Manila clam rocker.)

1011
00:39:02,655 --> 00:39:04,285
This is my third batch.

1012
00:39:04,285 --> 00:39:05,525
(It's already her third batch.)

1013
00:39:06,325 --> 00:39:09,365
(It's quite a huge pile.)

1014
00:39:09,925 --> 00:39:11,425
I don't even have to rake twice.

1015
00:39:12,295 --> 00:39:13,695
- Look at this. My goodness.
- I can do this, right?

1016
00:39:13,695 --> 00:39:15,035
(The siblings are harvesting clams in their own ways.)

1017
00:39:15,035 --> 00:39:17,435
- I hit a jackpot. This is a lot.
- I can do this.

1018
00:39:17,765 --> 00:39:20,175
- I can do this. I've got this.
- Oh, my.

1019
00:39:21,105 --> 00:39:23,105
- Yoon Seo, is it going well?
- Well...

1020
00:39:24,605 --> 00:39:25,775
- I'm not sure.
- This is amazing.

1021
00:39:26,345 --> 00:39:29,045
- Oh, there's a lot here.
- Picking them up is way faster.

1022
00:39:29,045 --> 00:39:31,285
- It's faster for us.
- Exactly.

1023
00:39:31,285 --> 00:39:32,655
They just keep coming out.

1024
00:39:34,655 --> 00:39:35,725
(Groaning)

1025
00:39:40,525 --> 00:39:42,055
(Her stool is stuck in the mud.)

1026
00:39:42,495 --> 00:39:44,965
(Laughing)

1027
00:39:45,125 --> 00:39:46,295
I can't get up.

1028
00:39:48,535 --> 00:39:50,005
(Stretching)

1029
00:39:51,435 --> 00:39:54,805
(What is that?)

1030
00:39:55,375 --> 00:39:57,175
You can't get up.

1031
00:39:57,175 --> 00:39:59,215
- It's hard to get up.
- It's not like that.

1032
00:39:59,215 --> 00:40:01,045
I'm stuck in the mud.

1033
00:40:01,045 --> 00:40:02,745
- What?
- Her stool is stuck in the mud.

1034
00:40:02,745 --> 00:40:03,915
(She became one with the mudflat.)

1035
00:40:04,915 --> 00:40:05,985
(Flustered)

1036
00:40:06,085 --> 00:40:07,255
Wait. I'll come to you.

1037
00:40:07,255 --> 00:40:08,985
(The two of them end up going to rescue her.)

1038
00:40:10,125 --> 00:40:12,995
(We're coming to rescue you.)

1039
00:40:13,195 --> 00:40:14,655
- Goodness, you.
- All I did was...

1040
00:40:14,655 --> 00:40:16,165
- work hard.
- She's completely stuck in the mud.

1041
00:40:16,295 --> 00:40:19,265
- I can't get up. Oh, thank you.
- Oh, gosh.

1042
00:40:20,135 --> 00:40:21,235
I just heard a popping sound.

1043
00:40:21,695 --> 00:40:24,635
- The mud is totally caved in.
- Hold on a second.

1044
00:40:25,305 --> 00:40:28,235
You must've sat there for so long seeing that you got stuck there.

1045
00:40:28,235 --> 00:40:29,475
(Sun Young left a legendary mark on the mudflat.)

1046
00:40:29,805 --> 00:40:31,875
Exactly. She must've sat in the same spot for so long.

1047
00:40:33,675 --> 00:40:35,215
Gosh, it's so heavy. I put too much in here.

1048
00:40:35,215 --> 00:40:36,245
(The biggest problem is...)

1049
00:40:36,245 --> 00:40:37,315
I put too much in here.

1050
00:40:38,515 --> 00:40:40,955
(The mud, soaked with water, is heavier than they expected.)

1051
00:40:41,655 --> 00:40:44,985
(The more they put in, the heavier it gets.)

1052
00:40:46,725 --> 00:40:47,725
Just...

1053
00:40:48,195 --> 00:40:49,565
making simple soup with these... My back hurts.

1054
00:40:49,565 --> 00:40:53,035
(On top of that, they have to stay bent over to dig up the clams.)

1055
00:40:53,465 --> 00:40:55,165
Gosh, I might end up with a hunched back at this rate.

1056
00:40:56,735 --> 00:40:58,465
(Staggering)

1057
00:40:58,975 --> 00:41:01,405
(Sitting down for so long, his legs gave up.)

1058
00:41:02,035 --> 00:41:03,075
Dear me.

1059
00:41:03,075 --> 00:41:05,005
(The siblings are starting to get tired.)

1060
00:41:05,645 --> 00:41:06,815
Jung Ah, this is hard.

1061
00:41:07,375 --> 00:41:10,315
Indeed. But there's no easy job in this world.

1062
00:41:10,315 --> 00:41:11,315
(There's no easy job in this world, but...)

1063
00:41:12,815 --> 00:41:16,725
(With no shade in this vast mudflat,)

1064
00:41:18,125 --> 00:41:23,595
(digging up hidden Manila clams is no easy feat.)

1065
00:41:24,695 --> 00:41:26,865
(What you need when you're getting tired is...)

1066
00:41:27,235 --> 00:41:30,835
One lighting under a dim light

1067
00:41:30,935 --> 00:41:32,005
It's "one candle."

1068
00:41:32,505 --> 00:41:33,675
- Oh, is it "candle?" - It's "candle."

1069
00:41:34,375 --> 00:41:36,145
Reflected on the wine glass is

1070
00:41:36,545 --> 00:41:38,445
- The world of Manila clams - A promise

1071
00:41:39,615 --> 00:41:40,875
The world of Manila clams

1072
00:41:42,315 --> 00:41:43,845
Many people choose this song for their wedding.

1073
00:41:44,285 --> 00:41:45,515
I'm sure a lot of people sing it at a wedding.

1074
00:41:46,815 --> 00:41:49,625
Jung Seok, have you sung at many weddings?

1075
00:41:49,625 --> 00:41:51,555
I've sung at a few weddings.

1076
00:41:52,595 --> 00:41:54,295
- They must've been so happy.
- I sang "Aloha."

1077
00:41:54,295 --> 00:41:55,725
- People must've loved hearing it.
- Exactly.

1078
00:41:56,395 --> 00:41:57,465
Even the guests.

1079
00:41:57,525 --> 00:41:58,525
Right?

1080
00:41:58,525 --> 00:42:00,595
- I...
- Can you sing a song at my wedding?

1081
00:42:00,595 --> 00:42:01,765
Here's...

1082
00:42:01,765 --> 00:42:03,735
(She's been married for 17 years.)

1083
00:42:03,765 --> 00:42:06,635
Here's an interesting story.

1084
00:42:07,335 --> 00:42:10,005
There was this producer I used to work with.

1085
00:42:10,345 --> 00:42:13,945
He asked me to sing at his wedding.

1086
00:42:14,245 --> 00:42:17,445
Back then, I had just gotten vision correction surgery.

1087
00:42:18,345 --> 00:42:20,785
I couldn't see anything and was told to keep my eyes closed.

1088
00:42:21,285 --> 00:42:22,355
Oh, dear.

1089
00:42:22,455 --> 00:42:25,385
I introduced Gummy instead.

1090
00:42:25,525 --> 00:42:26,895
You introduced Gummy?

1091
00:42:26,895 --> 00:42:29,995
When I did, the producer said, "Nice!"

1092
00:42:30,095 --> 00:42:31,095
(All the better)

1093
00:42:31,095 --> 00:42:32,165
He was over the moon.

1094
00:42:32,265 --> 00:42:35,335
(The ultimate wedding singer)

1095
00:42:36,035 --> 00:42:37,165
"Nice?"

1096
00:42:37,165 --> 00:42:39,105
Maybe he was actually after Gummy.

1097
00:42:39,105 --> 00:42:40,605
Yes, that's a possibility.

1098
00:42:41,175 --> 00:42:43,345
He couldn't ask Gummy himself.

1099
00:42:43,345 --> 00:42:45,175
- Of course not.
- He might come across as rude.

1100
00:42:45,175 --> 00:42:47,475
(A lively chat unfolds on the mudflat.)

1101
00:42:47,475 --> 00:42:49,285
- Goodness.
- This is fun.

1102
00:42:49,285 --> 00:42:50,645
(Optimistic Yoon Seo)

1103
00:42:50,645 --> 00:42:51,685
Isn't it fun?

1104
00:42:51,685 --> 00:42:53,455
- It is.
- Why...

1105
00:42:53,985 --> 00:42:55,455
Chatting makes it fun.

1106
00:42:55,455 --> 00:42:56,455
(Talking makes the hard work feel a little easier.)

1107
00:42:56,455 --> 00:42:57,455
How joyful.

1108
00:42:58,855 --> 00:43:02,695
Hey, Seok's dad. It's been a while...

1109
00:43:02,695 --> 00:43:04,165
since I last saw you here.

1110
00:43:04,495 --> 00:43:05,695
Sun Young.

1111
00:43:05,695 --> 00:43:06,865
- What?
- I'm Jung Ja.

1112
00:43:08,135 --> 00:43:09,205
A woman, okay?

1113
00:43:09,905 --> 00:43:11,205
Despite my husky voice.

1114
00:43:11,205 --> 00:43:13,975
- Were you a woman?
- Jung Ja, is it?

1115
00:43:13,975 --> 00:43:15,075
I didn't know.

1116
00:43:15,075 --> 00:43:16,645
Are you Jung Ja, not Seok's dad?

1117
00:43:16,645 --> 00:43:18,745
Jung Ja, do you still shave?

1118
00:43:19,145 --> 00:43:21,075
If only I had less hair, you know?

1119
00:43:21,115 --> 00:43:22,615
(Laughing)

1120
00:43:22,615 --> 00:43:23,985
It's impossible not to shave.

1121
00:43:24,415 --> 00:43:27,015
You Soon, you used to follow...

1122
00:43:27,015 --> 00:43:28,755
Jung Ja around all the time.

1123
00:43:28,755 --> 00:43:31,625
- Why are you being awkward now?
- Exactly. Didn't you miss her?

1124
00:43:31,625 --> 00:43:33,755
Why are you so quiet now that she's here?

1125
00:43:33,755 --> 00:43:36,195
- It's been a while, okay?
- She's all nervous.

1126
00:43:36,195 --> 00:43:37,765
- Exactly. I'm getting shy.
- Gosh.

1127
00:43:39,335 --> 00:43:40,665
I'm ready, okay?

1128
00:43:42,095 --> 00:43:43,705
(Jung Ja's sudden flirtation)

1129
00:43:43,705 --> 00:43:45,435
- Is your heart ready for me?
- Of course.

1130
00:43:45,435 --> 00:43:46,635
(The flirting game begins)

1131
00:43:46,875 --> 00:43:48,675
(You Soon realizes Jung Ja's feelings.)

1132
00:43:48,735 --> 00:43:51,045
Well, I'll see you later in the evening. Okay?

1133
00:43:52,575 --> 00:43:54,145
My gosh, how naughty.

1134
00:43:54,545 --> 00:43:56,445
- Two women in the evening?
- "Naughty?"

1135
00:43:56,845 --> 00:43:59,315
(You Soon only has eyes for Jung Ja.)

1136
00:43:59,715 --> 00:44:01,855
(Jung Ja doesn't hate it all that much.)

1137
00:44:01,855 --> 00:44:04,455
You must give me your number. Got it, You Soon?

1138
00:44:04,625 --> 00:44:05,995
(Getting shy)

1139
00:44:06,255 --> 00:44:07,495
- Can I?
- Go ahead.

1140
00:44:08,195 --> 00:44:09,395
"Can I?"

1141
00:44:09,395 --> 00:44:13,195
(Flirting flying left and right, this is "Mudflat Island.")

1142
00:44:13,595 --> 00:44:15,295
(Raking)

1143
00:44:15,295 --> 00:44:17,435
(Splashing)

1144
00:44:17,435 --> 00:44:19,635
(It's already been 1.5 hours since digging up Manila clams.)

1145
00:44:20,305 --> 00:44:22,905
(Raking slows to a crawl)

1146
00:44:23,575 --> 00:44:26,345
(Suddenly much quieter)

1147
00:44:28,315 --> 00:44:29,315
(Groaning)

1148
00:44:29,315 --> 00:44:30,315
My wrist hurts.

1149
00:44:31,485 --> 00:44:32,685
My back is killing me.

1150
00:44:32,685 --> 00:44:33,955
(Out of battery)

1151
00:44:33,955 --> 00:44:36,055
Is there any way to keep my back from hurting?

1152
00:44:38,155 --> 00:44:41,255
(The camera moves to get a good shot of Sun Young.)

1153
00:44:41,625 --> 00:44:43,595
Why are you suddenly rushing in on me?

1154
00:44:43,795 --> 00:44:44,995
For what?

1155
00:44:45,227 --> 00:44:48,327
(The camera moves to get a good shot of Sun Young.)

1156
00:44:48,697 --> 00:44:50,597
Why are you suddenly rushing in on me?

1157
00:44:50,897 --> 00:44:51,927
For what?

1158
00:44:51,927 --> 00:44:53,567
Didn't you stay far away earlier?

1159
00:44:53,567 --> 00:44:56,937
Why come when I'm lying down and not when I was working hard?

1160
00:44:57,267 --> 00:44:58,867
Get a shot of me working hard,

1161
00:44:58,867 --> 00:45:00,637
not when I'm taking a short break.

1162
00:45:01,177 --> 00:45:03,507
Really, the viewers will get the wrong idea.

1163
00:45:03,807 --> 00:45:04,807
Seriously, these people.

1164
00:45:04,807 --> 00:45:05,977
(Like a press conference)

1165
00:45:05,977 --> 00:45:07,317
They come swarming in on me.

1166
00:45:07,317 --> 00:45:08,377
I'm going to work hard!

1167
00:45:08,817 --> 00:45:10,447
I was working hard like this, you know?

1168
00:45:10,447 --> 00:45:11,447
(Working after a 10-second break)

1169
00:45:11,647 --> 00:45:13,917
(Back to digging with renewed energy)

1170
00:45:13,917 --> 00:45:16,257
- Take a break, Sun Young.
- What?

1171
00:45:16,257 --> 00:45:17,457
Take a break.

1172
00:45:17,857 --> 00:45:19,997
You should too, Jung Ah. Are you okay?

1173
00:45:20,227 --> 00:45:23,867
I don't know what taking a break is.

1174
00:45:24,597 --> 00:45:26,337
You should learn, Jung Ah.

1175
00:45:27,997 --> 00:45:29,167
My goodness.

1176
00:45:29,167 --> 00:45:30,307
(Even Captain Yum is running on empty...)

1177
00:45:30,307 --> 00:45:31,367
(after hours of backbreaking work.)

1178
00:45:31,367 --> 00:45:32,737
Oh, gosh. I'm tired.

1179
00:45:33,577 --> 00:45:34,607
This is tough.

1180
00:45:34,607 --> 00:45:36,147
(Glancing)

1181
00:45:36,147 --> 00:45:37,177
My leg hurts.

1182
00:45:37,177 --> 00:45:38,407
(Everyone is drained.)

1183
00:45:40,117 --> 00:45:42,077
How about we all take a break?

1184
00:45:42,587 --> 00:45:45,247
Should we take a break and play a game here on the mudflat?

1185
00:45:45,617 --> 00:45:46,657
What?

1186
00:45:46,657 --> 00:45:48,217
Should we take a break and play a game?

1187
00:45:48,557 --> 00:45:50,627
What kind of game do you have in mind?

1188
00:45:50,627 --> 00:45:52,697
Let's bet on something...

1189
00:45:54,257 --> 00:45:56,227
and play a game with these guys.

1190
00:45:56,227 --> 00:45:58,867
- What game?
- With the production staff?

1191
00:45:58,867 --> 00:45:59,897
Yes.

1192
00:46:00,237 --> 00:46:02,837
(The gamer puts on his thinking cap.)

1193
00:46:02,837 --> 00:46:03,867
Long jump?

1194
00:46:03,867 --> 00:46:04,907
(How about mudflat long jump?)

1195
00:46:04,907 --> 00:46:06,137
Let's do long jump.

1196
00:46:07,637 --> 00:46:08,737
Mudflat long jump.

1197
00:46:09,307 --> 00:46:12,007
As You Seok suggested,

1198
00:46:12,007 --> 00:46:13,217
how about a match of long jump?

1199
00:46:13,217 --> 00:46:14,247
Right here?

1200
00:46:14,647 --> 00:46:15,677
I'm in!

1201
00:46:16,147 --> 00:46:17,147
Okay!

1202
00:46:17,617 --> 00:46:19,787
If the five of you can jump...

1203
00:46:19,787 --> 00:46:23,127
a total of more than 5m, we'll give you 50 dollars.

1204
00:46:23,127 --> 00:46:24,827
- What?
- A total of 5m?

1205
00:46:24,827 --> 00:46:26,457
- Each has to jump 1m?
- The 5 of us?

1206
00:46:26,857 --> 00:46:27,927
Okay.

1207
00:46:28,057 --> 00:46:30,167
How do we pass 5m?

1208
00:46:30,867 --> 00:46:33,597
I doubt I can even jump 30cm.

1209
00:46:33,967 --> 00:46:35,397
How about we add ten dollars...

1210
00:46:35,397 --> 00:46:37,167
for every additional 1m you jump?

1211
00:46:37,167 --> 00:46:38,337
(10 dollars for every 1m?)

1212
00:46:39,107 --> 00:46:40,107
Nice.

1213
00:46:40,107 --> 00:46:41,107
(The production staff's shocking offer)

1214
00:46:41,107 --> 00:46:42,647
- Okay, 5m. Let's do it.
- Okay.

1215
00:46:42,647 --> 00:46:43,907
- Okay.
- So we get 50 dollars for 5m.

1216
00:46:43,907 --> 00:46:45,307
- And then 10 dollars per 1m.
- We can totally do it.

1217
00:46:45,777 --> 00:46:48,017
- Great.
- I'm taking my hat off.

1218
00:46:48,717 --> 00:46:49,787
Let's do this.

1219
00:46:51,187 --> 00:46:53,057
- Okay, let's go.
- We only have to jump 1m each.

1220
00:46:53,117 --> 00:46:54,217
- Let's go for it.
- Okay.

1221
00:46:54,457 --> 00:46:56,227
- Can we practice?
- Jump 5m, and we get 50 dollars.

1222
00:46:56,857 --> 00:46:57,857
Okay.

1223
00:46:57,857 --> 00:46:59,227
(The 1st Siblings' Mudflat Long Jump Competition)

1224
00:46:59,227 --> 00:47:00,527
That's the jump line.

1225
00:47:01,157 --> 00:47:02,897
This is the starting line.

1226
00:47:02,897 --> 00:47:05,097
You have to jump from here, the run-up spot.

1227
00:47:05,097 --> 00:47:07,837
Here. It's best to keep the run-up area hard.

1228
00:47:08,137 --> 00:47:09,167
The mud is so wet.

1229
00:47:09,737 --> 00:47:11,667
(Light splashing)

1230
00:47:11,667 --> 00:47:14,037
(Following You Seok)

1231
00:47:15,737 --> 00:47:18,247
(Extremely determined)

1232
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:20,477
- Good luck, Jung Ah.
- First. I'm going to jump.

1233
00:47:21,177 --> 00:47:22,477
- Okay.
- First jumper.

1234
00:47:22,477 --> 00:47:23,547
Good luck, Yum Jung Ah!

1235
00:47:24,617 --> 00:47:25,687
(Jumping line)

1236
00:47:25,687 --> 00:47:27,117
- Good luck.
- Let's go!

1237
00:47:28,017 --> 00:47:29,087
- Okay!
- Nice.

1238
00:47:29,117 --> 00:47:30,927
- Good luck!
- Let's go!

1239
00:47:31,627 --> 00:47:33,027
(Jumping lightly)

1240
00:47:33,027 --> 00:47:34,557
(After landing safely)

1241
00:47:34,557 --> 00:47:36,397
(An ending pose)

1242
00:47:36,797 --> 00:47:37,927
(Jung Ah's record)

1243
00:47:37,927 --> 00:47:39,067
It's 1.10m.

1244
00:47:39,067 --> 00:47:40,067
He said 1.10m.

1245
00:47:40,067 --> 00:47:41,737
(She passed 1m!)

1246
00:47:42,397 --> 00:47:43,607
Let's try for 60 dollars!

1247
00:47:44,167 --> 00:47:45,237
- Good job.
- Nice.

1248
00:47:45,237 --> 00:47:46,837
- You did your share.
- We could go for 60 dollars.

1249
00:47:46,837 --> 00:47:48,177
- We totally could.
- Second.

1250
00:47:48,177 --> 00:47:49,307
Second jumper.

1251
00:47:49,677 --> 00:47:51,707
Kim Sun Young, 51 years old.

1252
00:47:51,707 --> 00:47:53,017
- Good luck, Kim Sun Young!
- Let's go!

1253
00:47:54,147 --> 00:47:55,217
Go!

1254
00:47:55,217 --> 00:47:56,217
(Jumping line)

1255
00:47:56,217 --> 00:47:57,447
- Okay!
- Nice.

1256
00:47:58,287 --> 00:48:00,087
(Okay!)

1257
00:48:00,157 --> 00:48:01,917
- You two are good at it.
- Sun Young...

1258
00:48:04,087 --> 00:48:06,197
No, measure up...

1259
00:48:06,627 --> 00:48:07,997
to my heel.

1260
00:48:07,997 --> 00:48:09,467
- You stepped here.
- No.

1261
00:48:09,467 --> 00:48:11,797
- The end of the body is...
- I'll measure from here.

1262
00:48:12,427 --> 00:48:13,837
Come on, sir.

1263
00:48:14,537 --> 00:48:15,567
- Who is he?
- Gosh. You're harsh.

1264
00:48:15,567 --> 00:48:16,567
Aren't you...

1265
00:48:16,567 --> 00:48:19,037
- Who are you? Aren't we a family?
- mean?

1266
00:48:19,037 --> 00:48:20,237
- This is...
- Be a little nice.

1267
00:48:20,237 --> 00:48:21,577
Are you from an international organization?

1268
00:48:21,577 --> 00:48:22,907
- This isn't some...
- Are you a judge?

1269
00:48:22,907 --> 00:48:24,007
Are you certified?

1270
00:48:24,007 --> 00:48:25,107
It's 1.20m.

1271
00:48:25,307 --> 00:48:26,947
- He said 1.20m.
- It's still over 1m.

1272
00:48:27,017 --> 00:48:29,387
- What if I jump like 50cm?
- Here.

1273
00:48:29,387 --> 00:48:30,417
(Records, Total: 2.12m)

1274
00:48:30,417 --> 00:48:32,017
- Who...
- The rising star,

1275
00:48:32,017 --> 00:48:33,187
- Who is next? Me?
- Roh Yoon Seo.

1276
00:48:33,187 --> 00:48:35,317
- Introduce yourself.
- Third, Roh Yoon Seo!

1277
00:48:35,457 --> 00:48:37,287
- Okay.
- Wait, Yoon Seo!

1278
00:48:37,727 --> 00:48:39,497
Where do you plan on stepping off?

1279
00:48:42,227 --> 00:48:43,227
Sun Young!

1280
00:48:43,967 --> 00:48:45,527
Where are you going to step?

1281
00:48:45,527 --> 00:48:47,397
- I won't.
- That spot looks good.

1282
00:48:47,397 --> 00:48:48,567
- Step here, okay?
- Okay.

1283
00:48:48,567 --> 00:48:50,707
- Should I lie down over there?
- Stop.

1284
00:48:50,707 --> 00:48:51,707
(Packing the mud down)

1285
00:48:51,707 --> 00:48:52,907
(Feeling the pressure)

1286
00:48:54,377 --> 00:48:55,377
One, two.

1287
00:48:55,377 --> 00:48:56,607
(Will she jump far?)

1288
00:48:59,107 --> 00:49:02,617
(Jumping line)

1289
00:49:02,617 --> 00:49:04,147
- That was far.
- Yoon Seo jumped more than 1m.

1290
00:49:04,287 --> 00:49:05,447
She didn't step on the line, right?

1291
00:49:05,447 --> 00:49:07,257
Amazing, Yoon Seo!

1292
00:49:07,257 --> 00:49:08,257
(Well done, youngest!)

1293
00:49:08,257 --> 00:49:09,657
- It's 1.66m.
- What?

1294
00:49:09,657 --> 00:49:12,627
- Incredible.
- That's my height.

1295
00:49:12,627 --> 00:49:14,127
How did you jump so far?

1296
00:49:14,127 --> 00:49:15,197
Great job.

1297
00:49:15,297 --> 00:49:16,467
Amazing.

1298
00:49:16,467 --> 00:49:17,727
- We can do it.
- Yes, 3.70m.

1299
00:49:17,727 --> 00:49:19,367
You Seok, go last.

1300
00:49:19,367 --> 00:49:21,337
- Apparently, 5m was too short.
- Right?

1301
00:49:21,337 --> 00:49:22,737
They should've suggested 7m.

1302
00:49:22,737 --> 00:49:24,037
- Exactly.
- Yes.

1303
00:49:24,407 --> 00:49:26,537
- Isn't it 70 dollars if we jump 7m?
- Yes.

1304
00:49:26,777 --> 00:49:27,777
(Laughing)

1305
00:49:27,777 --> 00:49:30,807
How dare you look down on us!

1306
00:49:31,077 --> 00:49:33,277
(Dancing)

1307
00:49:33,517 --> 00:49:34,717
Fourth, Cho Jung Seok.

1308
00:49:37,887 --> 00:49:40,357
(Jumping line)

1309
00:49:40,357 --> 00:49:41,417
Unbelievable.

1310
00:49:42,857 --> 00:49:44,457
- Unbelievable.
- Unbelievable.

1311
00:49:44,457 --> 00:49:46,927
He flew. Jung Seok literally flew.

1312
00:49:47,197 --> 00:49:49,597
(Here's a replay of Jung Seok the Flyer.)

1313
00:49:49,667 --> 00:49:50,697
(Hup!)

1314
00:49:52,027 --> 00:49:54,767
(A quick grunt, followed by a smooth landing)

1315
00:49:55,037 --> 00:49:57,107
(Did you see that?)

1316
00:49:57,207 --> 00:49:58,307
It's 1.99m.

1317
00:49:58,307 --> 00:49:59,877
(Jung Seok's record: 1.99m)

1318
00:50:00,007 --> 00:50:01,237
- My gosh.
- Good.

1319
00:50:01,237 --> 00:50:02,437
You could even join the Summer Games.

1320
00:50:02,777 --> 00:50:04,747
- That was no joke.
- For real.

1321
00:50:05,777 --> 00:50:06,977
Was it 1.99m?

1322
00:50:06,977 --> 00:50:08,017
(The only jumper left)

1323
00:50:08,217 --> 00:50:10,217
Am I the last? The pressure.

1324
00:50:10,217 --> 00:50:11,547
I don't think I can jump 2m.

1325
00:50:11,547 --> 00:50:12,987
- Here I go.
- Okay.

1326
00:50:12,987 --> 00:50:13,987
(5th jumper, Kang You Seok)

1327
00:50:14,357 --> 00:50:15,987
(The farther You Seok jumps, the more money gets added!)

1328
00:50:15,987 --> 00:50:17,027
Go slow at first.

1329
00:50:17,027 --> 00:50:20,597
(Jumping line)

1330
00:50:20,727 --> 00:50:22,357
(What a good jump!)

1331
00:50:22,727 --> 00:50:24,797
(It was indeed a good jump, but...)

1332
00:50:24,797 --> 00:50:25,827
Okay.

1333
00:50:25,827 --> 00:50:28,067
- His hand.
- Hand?

1334
00:50:28,167 --> 00:50:30,037
- No.
- No, I didn't land on my hand.

1335
00:50:30,337 --> 00:50:33,707
(Not a chance.)

1336
00:50:34,037 --> 00:50:35,407
You jumped more than enough.

1337
00:50:35,407 --> 00:50:36,447
(You Seok jumped far even if he used his hand.)

1338
00:50:36,847 --> 00:50:38,207
It's 1.88m.

1339
00:50:38,607 --> 00:50:41,147
- Amazing.
- Cool, You Seok.

1340
00:50:41,147 --> 00:50:42,377
It would've been 2m...

1341
00:50:42,377 --> 00:50:43,587
- if he hadn't used his hand.
- You jumped the farthest.

1342
00:50:44,387 --> 00:50:45,987
- We get 70... No, 80 dollars.
- It was his hand.

1343
00:50:45,987 --> 00:50:47,017
(Records, Total: 7.65m)

1344
00:50:47,217 --> 00:50:48,287
(The 5 jumped a total of 7.65m.)

1345
00:50:48,287 --> 00:50:49,887
- The total is 7.65m.
- Is it 76.5 dollars?

1346
00:50:50,657 --> 00:50:51,827
That'll be 76...

1347
00:50:51,827 --> 00:50:54,057
- Give us 76.52 dollars.
- It's 76.5 dollars.

1348
00:50:54,057 --> 00:50:55,127
Seventy...

1349
00:50:56,927 --> 00:51:00,837
(Earned another 20 dollars from a bonus game)

1350
00:51:00,837 --> 00:51:03,167
I spinned. You saw me spin, right?

1351
00:51:03,237 --> 00:51:04,337
Great job, everyone.

1352
00:51:04,337 --> 00:51:06,067
- Okay.
- Okay, thank you.

1353
00:51:07,337 --> 00:51:09,237
- Let's go.
- Yes, let's get going.

1354
00:51:09,947 --> 00:51:11,547
- Let's work.
- Hurry.

1355
00:51:11,547 --> 00:51:13,347
(Let's dig up more clams before the tide comes in!)

1356
00:51:14,547 --> 00:51:17,447
(The siblings are back to digging up clams after a sweet break.)

1357
00:51:18,317 --> 00:51:21,517
(Raking as fast as before thanks to the break)

1358
00:51:24,587 --> 00:51:27,457
(The second is practically getting sucked into the mudflat.)

1359
00:51:28,027 --> 00:51:30,227
I spot many here. Yes!

1360
00:51:34,037 --> 00:51:35,167
I'm tired.

1361
00:51:36,037 --> 00:51:37,107
No, I'm not.

1362
00:51:37,237 --> 00:51:38,367
(Losing it)

1363
00:51:38,367 --> 00:51:39,437
I'm not tired.

1364
00:51:40,407 --> 00:51:42,977
This may look easy.

1365
00:51:43,877 --> 00:51:46,217
But look, the clams are deep down.

1366
00:51:48,147 --> 00:51:49,347
The sun is rising.

1367
00:51:50,617 --> 00:51:51,947
It's rising just as we'll be leaving soon.

1368
00:51:53,017 --> 00:51:54,317
(As if the work wasn't hard enough,)

1369
00:51:54,317 --> 00:51:56,327
(the sun is scorching hot.)

1370
00:51:58,157 --> 00:51:59,627
It's hard, isn't it?

1371
00:52:00,027 --> 00:52:01,757
At least you're young with muscles.

1372
00:52:02,227 --> 00:52:03,267
Oh, dear.

1373
00:52:04,367 --> 00:52:08,197
(The clams show up after repeated digging.)

1374
00:52:08,197 --> 00:52:09,607
(Get as much as possible before the tide comes in!)

1375
00:52:09,607 --> 00:52:10,807
It's tiring.

1376
00:52:13,337 --> 00:52:17,007
I want to see how the experts dig up the clams.

1377
00:52:17,007 --> 00:52:19,547
- Right, Sun Young?
- I wonder how fast they are.

1378
00:52:19,547 --> 00:52:20,747
(Curious about the experts' speed)

1379
00:52:21,347 --> 00:52:22,447
I can see them from here.

1380
00:52:23,017 --> 00:52:24,247
They're no joke.

1381
00:52:24,247 --> 00:52:26,217
(Even from afar, it's obvious their speed is on another level.)

1382
00:52:26,817 --> 00:52:29,287
(Shall we take a look at the Manila clam seniors?)

1383
00:52:30,457 --> 00:52:33,327
(With speed on another level)

1384
00:52:34,357 --> 00:52:36,967
(Years of experience show in every rake)

1385
00:52:37,727 --> 00:52:40,537
(This is the strength of the seniors.)

1386
00:52:41,237 --> 00:52:42,967
This isn't an easy job.

1387
00:52:43,137 --> 00:52:45,207
Anyone would do it if it were easy.

1388
00:52:46,537 --> 00:52:48,907
Oh, gosh. I wonder how the ladies dig them up so well.

1389
00:52:48,907 --> 00:52:50,747
(Appreciating the seniors' hard work even more)

1390
00:52:50,747 --> 00:52:51,777
They're amazing.

1391
00:52:52,477 --> 00:52:56,077
Those ladies are incredible. I'm serious.

1392
00:52:57,487 --> 00:52:59,047
I didn't know clam digging was this hard.

1393
00:53:00,087 --> 00:53:01,487
I will eat them with appreciation now.

1394
00:53:02,287 --> 00:53:03,357
For real.

1395
00:53:03,457 --> 00:53:05,727
I will devour the clams in the Manila clam kalguksu.

1396
00:53:07,157 --> 00:53:08,457
Digging for them is hard.

1397
00:53:08,457 --> 00:53:10,527
(Every clam is a labor of love.)

1398
00:53:11,527 --> 00:53:13,997
(After carefully digging the clams up)

1399
00:53:14,297 --> 00:53:16,907
- Will the tide come in soon?
- Yes, it's already coming in.

1400
00:53:16,907 --> 00:53:18,367
(Not much time left before the tide returns)

1401
00:53:18,867 --> 00:53:20,177
- Already?
- Yes.

1402
00:53:20,737 --> 00:53:21,877
- Guys.
- Hurry.

1403
00:53:21,877 --> 00:53:23,477
We've got to dig up at least another kilogram.

1404
00:53:23,477 --> 00:53:25,607
- Three dollars.
- Three dollars.

1405
00:53:26,317 --> 00:53:29,047
- I've hit a jackpot here!
- A jackpot.

1406
00:53:29,217 --> 00:53:30,347
I'm going over, okay?

1407
00:53:30,347 --> 00:53:31,687
(Let's go for the last spurt!)

1408
00:53:32,317 --> 00:53:33,357
Oh, my.

1409
00:53:33,887 --> 00:53:35,687
It's heavy, isn't it?

1410
00:53:36,857 --> 00:53:39,127
This spot is filled with holes.

1411
00:53:40,057 --> 00:53:45,227
(All five speed it up.)

1412
00:53:46,467 --> 00:53:47,597
Okay.

1413
00:53:49,737 --> 00:53:51,537
Since it's a drop shipment,

1414
00:53:51,537 --> 00:53:53,007
- the clams we dig up...
- Exactly.

1415
00:53:53,007 --> 00:53:55,307
will be sold somewhere, and the viewers will make...

1416
00:53:55,307 --> 00:53:56,907
- Manila clam kalguksu out of them.
- Yes.

1417
00:53:57,077 --> 00:53:59,347
- Even make doenjang jjigae.
- Like so.

1418
00:53:59,447 --> 00:54:02,177
Here. Premium Manila clams.

1419
00:54:02,177 --> 00:54:03,247
See this?

1420
00:54:04,117 --> 00:54:05,647
Two, three, four.

1421
00:54:05,947 --> 00:54:07,557
When will I ever experience this?

1422
00:54:08,017 --> 00:54:10,387
It will become a legacy, an asset,

1423
00:54:10,587 --> 00:54:12,657
and a life experience.

1424
00:54:12,657 --> 00:54:14,627
The roots, the seeds, and the tree.

1425
00:54:15,857 --> 00:54:18,697
Eventually, an apple and an apple pie.

1426
00:54:20,667 --> 00:54:22,937
(Driving by)

1427
00:54:24,107 --> 00:54:25,867
(Lost in the work,)

1428
00:54:25,867 --> 00:54:27,577
(the tractors head home one by one.)

1429
00:54:28,707 --> 00:54:32,147
The tractors are starting up one by one.

1430
00:54:33,947 --> 00:54:35,377
(The tractors leaving mean...)

1431
00:54:35,377 --> 00:54:37,717
(the tide will come in any time soon.)

1432
00:54:38,217 --> 00:54:40,757
(We should also go back to land.)

1433
00:54:42,617 --> 00:54:46,497
(The siblings gather to weigh the clams.)

1434
00:54:47,097 --> 00:54:49,927
(Splitting the clams into bags)

1435
00:54:50,097 --> 00:54:51,097
All done.

1436
00:54:51,097 --> 00:54:52,867
Remember I said it was three dollars per kilogram?

1437
00:54:52,867 --> 00:54:53,937
Yes.

1438
00:54:54,297 --> 00:54:56,637
(Weighing the first bag)

1439
00:54:56,637 --> 00:54:57,767
It's 10kg.

1440
00:54:57,767 --> 00:54:59,977
(The 1st bag weighs 9.6kg.)

1441
00:55:01,177 --> 00:55:03,207
(The second bag weighs...)

1442
00:55:03,207 --> 00:55:04,577
It's 8.2kg.

1443
00:55:04,577 --> 00:55:06,717
(8.2kg.)

1444
00:55:07,317 --> 00:55:09,217
- This one is the heaviest.
- How much in total?

1445
00:55:09,217 --> 00:55:11,087
These are the first clams I dug up.

1446
00:55:12,017 --> 00:55:13,817
How heavy is it?

1447
00:55:13,817 --> 00:55:14,887
Is it 20kg?

1448
00:55:15,017 --> 00:55:17,057
Take your hands off the bag, please.

1449
00:55:17,057 --> 00:55:19,287
- Sorry?
- Stop with the dirty tricks.

1450
00:55:19,287 --> 00:55:20,627
(The scale drops as soon as he lets go.)

1451
00:55:20,827 --> 00:55:22,357
- It's 12.6kg.
- Right?

1452
00:55:22,357 --> 00:55:23,767
(The 3rd bag is 12.6kg.)

1453
00:55:24,627 --> 00:55:29,497
(Done digging up at a total of 30.4kg)

1454
00:55:29,737 --> 00:55:31,767
- How much is it?
- Three times three is nine.

1455
00:55:31,767 --> 00:55:33,037
- Is it 90 dollars?
- It's 90 dollars.

1456
00:55:33,037 --> 00:55:34,537
- That just now was...
- Ninety dollars.

1457
00:55:35,337 --> 00:55:36,947
How much is the grand total?

1458
00:55:37,307 --> 00:55:39,007
It's 180 dollars.

1459
00:55:39,877 --> 00:55:40,917
Really?

1460
00:55:41,047 --> 00:55:42,347
Imagine the amount...

1461
00:55:42,347 --> 00:55:44,447
- Sun Young...
- if we hadn't played long jump.

1462
00:55:44,447 --> 00:55:47,617
I thought 60kg of clams would be easy peasy.

1463
00:55:48,387 --> 00:55:51,427
We can't possibly dig up 60kg.

1464
00:55:51,427 --> 00:55:52,527
- Exactly.
- It sure is tough.

1465
00:55:52,527 --> 00:55:53,697
That wouldn't have cut it.

1466
00:55:54,527 --> 00:55:57,067
- Thank you!
- Thank you.

1467
00:55:57,067 --> 00:55:59,127
You had it tough in the heat.

1468
00:55:59,127 --> 00:56:00,697
- Thank you.
- Did you earn a lot?

1469
00:56:00,697 --> 00:56:01,897
- Yes.
- Thank you.

1470
00:56:01,967 --> 00:56:04,137
Clean clams for you to eat. After all, they're in season.

1471
00:56:04,137 --> 00:56:05,167
Can we eat them right away?

1472
00:56:05,167 --> 00:56:06,307
- Yes.
- Thank you.

1473
00:56:06,307 --> 00:56:07,377
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1474
00:56:07,377 --> 00:56:09,207
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1475
00:56:09,207 --> 00:56:11,377
- They've already been purged.
- Really?

1476
00:56:11,377 --> 00:56:13,547
- Thank you.
- We can eat them right away.

1477
00:56:13,547 --> 00:56:14,977
(Purged Manila clams will be served today.)

1478
00:56:16,347 --> 00:56:19,447
It feels pretty rewarding to have dug up that many clams.

1479
00:56:20,087 --> 00:56:21,857
(Staring)

1480
00:56:21,857 --> 00:56:23,627
Look at all those holes.

1481
00:56:24,857 --> 00:56:26,357
- All I can see are the holes.
- Right?

1482
00:56:28,427 --> 00:56:30,097
Those are all siphon openings.

1483
00:56:31,367 --> 00:56:32,567
Mudflats are tough.

1484
00:56:32,567 --> 00:56:35,537
- My legs are starting to give way.
- Right?

1485
00:56:35,537 --> 00:56:37,907
My back and hands took quite a beating.

1486
00:56:38,567 --> 00:56:40,177
- We're back on land.
- We're here.

1487
00:56:40,177 --> 00:56:42,477
(They arrived on land before they knew it.)

1488
00:56:44,047 --> 00:56:45,507
The clams are cleaned immediately over here.

1489
00:56:46,107 --> 00:56:49,217
(Right next to where the tractors come in)

1490
00:56:49,847 --> 00:56:51,917
(The clam washing and sorting station)

1491
00:56:52,747 --> 00:56:55,957
(The clams we harvested today are...)

1492
00:56:57,057 --> 00:57:01,327
(washed and sorted by size here.)

1493
00:57:02,297 --> 00:57:05,827
(Squeaky clean)

1494
00:57:06,797 --> 00:57:10,407
(Packed into 20kg bags,)

1495
00:57:11,107 --> 00:57:14,737
(the fresh clams are...)

1496
00:57:15,207 --> 00:57:17,377
(shipped straight to destinations across the country.)

1497
00:57:18,207 --> 00:57:24,147
(The siblings wash off the mud at the tap.)

1498
00:57:24,917 --> 00:57:28,217
(His mischievous face says it all.)

1499
00:57:32,927 --> 00:57:34,127
(Annoyed)

1500
00:57:34,757 --> 00:57:35,997
(2nd time)

1501
00:57:35,997 --> 00:57:37,767
(3rd time)

1502
00:57:38,367 --> 00:57:40,767
(Are you trying me?)

1503
00:57:41,937 --> 00:57:43,167
(Here's my revenge!)

1504
00:57:46,637 --> 00:57:47,937
(Monkey mode on)

1505
00:57:48,437 --> 00:57:50,877
(A full-scale water fight breaks out.)

1506
00:57:52,147 --> 00:57:55,717
(For a moment, they're kids again.)

1507
00:57:57,217 --> 00:58:00,757
(A water fight is enough to make these siblings happy.)

1508
00:58:01,757 --> 00:58:02,817
Oh, gosh.

1509
00:58:03,727 --> 00:58:04,787
Oh, gosh.

1510
00:58:07,357 --> 00:58:10,097
(Feeling happy just by watching them)

1511
00:58:10,427 --> 00:58:11,527
How young.

1512
00:58:12,867 --> 00:58:13,937
You sure are young.

1513
00:58:13,937 --> 00:58:15,867
This is fun. A water fight is fun.

1514
00:58:15,867 --> 00:58:17,707
(The siblings cooled down with a water fight.)

1515
00:58:18,367 --> 00:58:20,837
I'm sleepy. I need to fill in my brows.

1516
00:58:20,837 --> 00:58:22,277
(After digging up the clams)

1517
00:58:22,907 --> 00:58:24,247
(Spotted the camera)

1518
00:58:24,247 --> 00:58:26,917
Dear viewers, we're not one bit tired.

1519
00:58:27,577 --> 00:58:28,977
We're back after a shower.

1520
00:58:28,977 --> 00:58:31,087
You see my bare brows? A shocker, right?

1521
00:58:31,447 --> 00:58:34,217
(The viewers are Sun Young's energizer.)

1522
00:58:34,517 --> 00:58:36,017
Let's check my brows.

1523
00:58:36,317 --> 00:58:37,927
I'm not sure if I can fill them in...

1524
00:58:37,927 --> 00:58:39,087
when the car is moving.

1525
00:58:39,557 --> 00:58:40,627
Before filling in my brows,

1526
00:58:40,627 --> 00:58:42,827
- let's apply something to my face.
- Seventeen minutes.

1527
00:58:42,827 --> 00:58:44,367
- Seventeen minutes.
- That's plenty of time.

1528
00:58:44,367 --> 00:58:45,427
Seventeen minutes.

1529
00:58:45,927 --> 00:58:47,597
Yoon Seo, let's make a list of the groceries to buy.

1530
00:58:47,837 --> 00:58:49,097
- List the groceries?
- Yes.

1531
00:58:49,097 --> 00:58:50,437
- Okay.
- Our grocery list.

1532
00:58:50,437 --> 00:58:51,467
Got it.

1533
00:58:51,707 --> 00:58:53,067
Meat for tangsuyuk.

1534
00:58:53,537 --> 00:58:55,977
- Cucumbers. We need cucumbers.
- Give me a second.

1535
00:58:56,907 --> 00:58:58,507
- Cucumbers.
- Cucumbers.

1536
00:58:59,277 --> 00:59:01,147
Meat for tangsuyuk.

1537
00:59:01,577 --> 00:59:03,047
- Pork sirloin.
- Meat for tangsuyuk.

1538
00:59:03,617 --> 00:59:05,047
Jjamppong.

1539
00:59:05,647 --> 00:59:06,717
Seafood.

1540
00:59:06,717 --> 00:59:08,817
- We only have Manila clams.
- Seafood.

1541
00:59:09,157 --> 00:59:11,687
And then, let's move on to pepper japchae.

1542
00:59:11,857 --> 00:59:12,857
- Okay.
- Gosh.

1543
00:59:12,857 --> 00:59:14,497
- Pepper japchae sounds good.
- Right?

1544
00:59:14,797 --> 00:59:16,557
- Flower buns.
- Flower buns.

1545
00:59:17,197 --> 00:59:18,527
We need flower buns.

1546
00:59:18,527 --> 00:59:19,697
(A spectacular Chinese feast is coming soon.)

1547
00:59:19,697 --> 00:59:22,337
Bell peppers, onions, and you wrote that down, right?

1548
00:59:22,997 --> 00:59:25,667
Let's buy zucchini and button mushrooms if there are any.

1549
00:59:25,737 --> 00:59:26,777
- Okay.
- Okay.

1550
00:59:26,777 --> 00:59:28,107
They're good inside jjamppong.

1551
00:59:29,337 --> 00:59:31,077
Let's play Word Chain. Zucchini.

1552
00:59:32,777 --> 00:59:34,277
- Ni, Jung Ah.
- Ni?

1553
00:59:34,277 --> 00:59:35,517
(All of a sudden?)

1554
00:59:35,947 --> 00:59:37,717
Five, four, three, two, one.

1555
00:59:37,717 --> 00:59:38,917
- Bye.
- Bye.

1556
00:59:38,917 --> 00:59:40,487
- What's there with an "Ni?" - Nice.

1557
00:59:40,817 --> 00:59:42,087
- Three syllables?
- Two or three?

1558
00:59:42,087 --> 00:59:44,227
Three. We'll go clockwise, starting with Jung Ah.

1559
00:59:44,227 --> 00:59:45,757
- It's Jung Seok after me.
- Okay.

1560
00:59:45,757 --> 00:59:47,657
- You can't say nice.
- Restart.

1561
00:59:47,857 --> 00:59:49,327
- No nice.
- Come on.

1562
00:59:49,327 --> 00:59:50,797
(Officially starting Word Chain)

1563
00:59:50,797 --> 00:59:52,767
- Shall we do it in Chinese?
- What?

1564
00:59:52,927 --> 00:59:54,097
Chinese?

1565
00:59:54,097 --> 00:59:55,337
(Officially starting Chinese Word Chain)

1566
00:59:55,537 --> 00:59:56,737
I only know "xiexie."

1567
00:59:56,737 --> 00:59:57,737
(Speaking gibberish)

1568
00:59:59,367 --> 01:00:00,377
(Speaking gibberish)

1569
01:00:00,707 --> 01:00:01,737
What is that?

1570
01:00:01,737 --> 01:00:04,177
- Only the intonation is in Chinese.
- Correct.

1571
01:00:04,177 --> 01:00:06,147
- Chinese intonation?
- Here's how you do it.

1572
01:00:06,147 --> 01:00:08,047
If I say "wo shi ah," Jung Ah has to start with...

1573
01:00:08,047 --> 01:00:09,547
"ah." Go ahead.

1574
01:00:09,717 --> 01:00:10,987
"Ah ye."

1575
01:00:11,247 --> 01:00:12,687
"Ye?"

1576
01:00:13,247 --> 01:00:15,387
Ye he le.

1577
01:00:15,657 --> 01:00:17,087
Confidence is what you need.

1578
01:00:17,527 --> 01:00:18,727
Yes, confidence.

1579
01:00:18,827 --> 01:00:20,897
Let's try it.

1580
01:00:21,057 --> 01:00:22,657
You start, Jung Ah.

1581
01:00:22,657 --> 01:00:24,967
(Speaking fake Chinese)

1582
01:00:25,127 --> 01:00:26,197
Huo la ha yi.

1583
01:00:26,297 --> 01:00:28,097
"Yi." Start with an "yi."

1584
01:00:28,397 --> 01:00:29,537
Yi er san.

1585
01:00:30,137 --> 01:00:32,307
(Nice one!)

1586
01:00:32,767 --> 01:00:33,907
San cha ho yi.

1587
01:00:34,477 --> 01:00:35,777
"Yi." It's "yi" again.

1588
01:00:36,277 --> 01:00:37,377
Yi hong shi.

1589
01:00:37,677 --> 01:00:38,847
- "Shi?" - "Shi."

1590
01:00:39,107 --> 01:00:41,377
Shi pea ker.

1591
01:00:41,517 --> 01:00:43,317
- Isn't that an alien language?
- That just now..

1592
01:00:43,587 --> 01:00:45,647
- That sounded Korean.
- That's English.

1593
01:00:45,647 --> 01:00:46,717
- No.
- Out.

1594
01:00:47,057 --> 01:00:48,417
- It made sense, so bye.
- Hold on.

1595
01:00:48,417 --> 01:00:49,587
If it makes sense, you're out.

1596
01:00:49,787 --> 01:00:51,657
(Do it properly.)

1597
01:00:52,427 --> 01:00:54,157
Let's stop here.

1598
01:00:54,457 --> 01:00:57,397
Now, let's move on to Japan.

1599
01:00:57,397 --> 01:00:59,167
- Japan.
- I'm confident in that.

1600
01:00:59,167 --> 01:01:01,197
- I'm confident.
- I can really do Japanese.

1601
01:01:01,197 --> 01:01:03,237
But you can't speak actual Japanese.

1602
01:01:03,237 --> 01:01:04,437
- Really?
- Fake Japanese...

1603
01:01:04,437 --> 01:01:05,467
but make it sound real.

1604
01:01:05,467 --> 01:01:07,607
- Then I'm in a bind.
- Okay.

1605
01:01:08,437 --> 01:01:09,607
You can start.

1606
01:01:11,477 --> 01:01:12,477
Imakano.

1607
01:01:12,677 --> 01:01:14,747
- That was good.
- Imakano.

1608
01:01:14,747 --> 01:01:16,987
- Imakano was good.
- "No."

1609
01:01:17,787 --> 01:01:20,217
Nogodouri...

1610
01:01:20,787 --> 01:01:22,117
- Nogodouri.
- Nogodouri.

1611
01:01:22,357 --> 01:01:24,657
Yorushikare.

1612
01:01:24,957 --> 01:01:26,897
Why is a word so long? That's a sentence.

1613
01:01:27,657 --> 01:01:28,997
Norikashine.

1614
01:01:30,167 --> 01:01:31,497
- Omashai...
- Norikashine.

1615
01:01:31,497 --> 01:01:32,497
- Omagaishine.
- I can't draw my eyebrows...

1616
01:01:32,497 --> 01:01:33,497
because he's so funny.

1617
01:01:33,497 --> 01:01:35,497
I can't draw one side of my eyebrows because I'm laughing.

1618
01:01:36,437 --> 01:01:38,467
- Omagaisa. "Sa." - "Sa."

1619
01:01:38,467 --> 01:01:39,837
(His speech has finally ended.)

1620
01:01:40,207 --> 01:01:42,407
- Saichi.
- Saichi.

1621
01:01:42,407 --> 01:01:44,147
- Saichi.
- What is it again?

1622
01:01:44,147 --> 01:01:45,307
- "Chi." - Chi?"

1623
01:01:47,147 --> 01:01:48,317
Chikino meogo sipo.

1624
01:01:48,977 --> 01:01:50,147
- You want to eat fried chicken?
- You want to eat fried chicken?

1625
01:01:51,117 --> 01:01:53,287
You can't speak Korean.

1626
01:01:53,287 --> 01:01:55,757
I thought I just needed to avoid speaking actual Japanese.

1627
01:01:55,757 --> 01:01:56,757
Say it again.

1628
01:01:56,757 --> 01:01:59,387
- Chikino meogo sipo.
- You want to eat fried chicken?

1629
01:01:59,987 --> 01:02:00,997
I'll let it slide once.

1630
01:02:01,097 --> 01:02:02,197
- Is it "po?" - "Po."

1631
01:02:02,197 --> 01:02:03,197
"Po."

1632
01:02:04,027 --> 01:02:06,837
(Po?)

1633
01:02:06,997 --> 01:02:07,997
Porigato.

1634
01:02:09,467 --> 01:02:11,667
- Arigato?
- I said porigato!

1635
01:02:11,737 --> 01:02:12,737
Porigato.

1636
01:02:12,737 --> 01:02:13,777
(Denying it to the grave)

1637
01:02:13,777 --> 01:02:14,837
Porigato.

1638
01:02:16,537 --> 01:02:17,607
"To."

1639
01:02:17,607 --> 01:02:18,607
(She continues the game as if nothing happened.)

1640
01:02:18,607 --> 01:02:19,847
(Look at her.)

1641
01:02:19,847 --> 01:02:20,917
(You're a lunatic.)

1642
01:02:20,917 --> 01:02:22,477
(Found guilty)

1643
01:02:23,217 --> 01:02:25,187
(Jung Ah-chan once again ends the game.)

1644
01:02:25,747 --> 01:02:27,387
(Sun Young is eliminated.)

1645
01:02:27,857 --> 01:02:28,857
Let's do Russian.

1646
01:02:29,387 --> 01:02:31,727
- Let's play it one last time.
- You sure?

1647
01:02:31,727 --> 01:02:34,457
- Russian or French?
- Sun Young. Then can I...

1648
01:02:35,197 --> 01:02:36,727
I have a question.

1649
01:02:37,997 --> 01:02:39,897
- When will you draw your eyebrow?
- My eyebrow.

1650
01:02:39,897 --> 01:02:42,567
- Draw when the car has stopped.
- You're right.

1651
01:02:42,967 --> 01:02:45,607
- We're almost there.
- I need to draw this side too.

1652
01:02:46,267 --> 01:02:47,777
My eyebrows are uneven.

1653
01:02:47,777 --> 01:02:48,777
It's okay.

1654
01:02:52,007 --> 01:02:54,117
It's a traditional market.

1655
01:02:54,117 --> 01:02:55,577
- That's where we're going?
- Yes.

1656
01:02:56,947 --> 01:02:58,017
"Taean Seobu Market."

1657
01:02:58,017 --> 01:02:59,187
(As they laugh and talk, they arrive at the market.)

1658
01:02:59,487 --> 01:03:00,687
- What's this?
- Small octopus.

1659
01:03:00,687 --> 01:03:01,757
They're as big as normal octopus.

1660
01:03:01,957 --> 01:03:02,987
Look at the razor shell.

1661
01:03:02,987 --> 01:03:03,987
(Octopus-like huge small octopuses to gigantic razor shells)

1662
01:03:04,487 --> 01:03:06,387
(As expected of Taean, a maritime city,)

1663
01:03:06,387 --> 01:03:08,257
(it's full of fresh seafood.)

1664
01:03:09,257 --> 01:03:13,327
(They have freshly-dug Manila clams too.)

1665
01:03:13,737 --> 01:03:14,767
It's pretty big.

1666
01:03:14,767 --> 01:03:15,797
(From an old-fashioned hair salon...)

1667
01:03:15,797 --> 01:03:17,907
(to snacks)

1668
01:03:18,537 --> 01:03:23,077
(The traditional market feels very friendly and cozy.)

1669
01:03:23,677 --> 01:03:24,677
- You Seok.
- Yes?

1670
01:03:24,677 --> 01:03:26,007
I have eyebrows now. Look.

1671
01:03:26,677 --> 01:03:27,747
You got prettier.

1672
01:03:27,747 --> 01:03:28,847
(Her eyebrows are ready in time.)

1673
01:03:29,417 --> 01:03:30,647
(Expectant)

1674
01:03:31,687 --> 01:03:33,347
- Sea squirt.
- Hello.

1675
01:03:33,347 --> 01:03:35,187
Hello. Manila clams.

1676
01:03:35,187 --> 01:03:37,127
Sea squirts.

1677
01:03:38,327 --> 01:03:39,987
Wild sea squirts.

1678
01:03:39,987 --> 01:03:41,227
(Sea squirts they met in Tongyeong)

1679
01:03:41,557 --> 01:03:43,457
The cuttlefish looks so cute.

1680
01:03:44,827 --> 01:03:45,867
My gosh.

1681
01:03:45,867 --> 01:03:47,367
(The market is full of fascinating and delicious things.)

1682
01:03:48,897 --> 01:03:50,937
- Shall we eat that?
- Shall we eat street food?

1683
01:03:50,937 --> 01:03:53,137
- Let's eat fishcake and tteokbokki.
- Hello.

1684
01:03:53,567 --> 01:03:56,107
- Let's eat first.
- Let's eat.

1685
01:03:56,207 --> 01:03:58,277
- I can't walk past this.
- This is so...

1686
01:03:58,507 --> 01:04:01,017
- I want a corn dog.
- A corn dog?

1687
01:04:01,677 --> 01:04:02,747
I want fishcake.

1688
01:04:03,547 --> 01:04:06,087
- Deep-fried squid and gimmari too.
- Okay.

1689
01:04:06,087 --> 01:04:07,317
One deep-fried vegetable too.

1690
01:04:08,317 --> 01:04:10,757
Give us one plate of tteokbokki too, please.

1691
01:04:11,227 --> 01:04:12,287
Please give us a lot.

1692
01:04:13,257 --> 01:04:15,497
(She drinks the fishcake soup while waiting for the food.)

1693
01:04:16,157 --> 01:04:17,827
The soup is really good.

1694
01:04:18,727 --> 01:04:20,467
The soup is so good. My gosh.

1695
01:04:21,067 --> 01:04:22,237
(Surprised)

1696
01:04:23,907 --> 01:04:24,967
(Amazed)

1697
01:04:25,467 --> 01:04:28,137
(The addictive taste never fails you.)

1698
01:04:28,237 --> 01:04:30,947
Now that I've tasted the soup, I want to eat fishcake too.

1699
01:04:30,947 --> 01:04:32,007
I should eat one.

1700
01:04:32,007 --> 01:04:33,207
Thank you.

1701
01:04:35,017 --> 01:04:36,017
It's good.

1702
01:04:36,017 --> 01:04:37,447
(Enough with the appetizer, the real deal starts now.)

1703
01:04:37,447 --> 01:04:38,487
It's good.

1704
01:04:40,017 --> 01:04:41,087
(Humming)

1705
01:04:42,317 --> 01:04:43,387
Guys, eat this.

1706
01:04:45,227 --> 01:04:48,457
(Eating tteokbokki hurriedly)

1707
01:04:50,867 --> 01:04:52,767
(She's amazed by the taste.)

1708
01:04:53,467 --> 01:04:55,837
(Getting out of control)

1709
01:04:56,097 --> 01:04:57,137
I can't stop eating.

1710
01:04:57,137 --> 01:04:58,307
(Taking another bite)

1711
01:04:59,537 --> 01:05:00,537
- It's good, right?
- Yes.

1712
01:05:01,007 --> 01:05:02,077
It's delicious.

1713
01:05:03,007 --> 01:05:04,677
It's so delicious.

1714
01:05:04,677 --> 01:05:05,707
(Happy)

1715
01:05:06,307 --> 01:05:07,977
I know him.

1716
01:05:08,777 --> 01:05:11,747
- Gummy. His wife is Gummy.
- That's right.

1717
01:05:12,247 --> 01:05:14,387
- I used to like Gummy.
- Thank you.

1718
01:05:14,387 --> 01:05:16,317
- This...
- I like Gummy too.

1719
01:05:16,317 --> 01:05:18,157
(Laughing)

1720
01:05:18,327 --> 01:05:19,757
Gummy's husband first.

1721
01:05:19,757 --> 01:05:20,857
Thank you.

1722
01:05:22,127 --> 01:05:23,197
It's freshly deep-fried.

1723
01:05:24,627 --> 01:05:26,497
(Crunchy)

1724
01:05:27,297 --> 01:05:32,207
(Thanks to Gummy's husband, they get to enjoy it all the more.)

1725
01:05:32,767 --> 01:05:33,807
It's so good but hot.

1726
01:05:35,107 --> 01:05:36,437
- It's so good.
- Yes.

1727
01:05:37,077 --> 01:05:38,507
This deep-fried squid is on the house.

1728
01:05:38,507 --> 01:05:39,807
- Gosh, thank you.
- Thank you.

1729
01:05:39,807 --> 01:05:41,077
I should give one for Gummy's husband.

1730
01:05:41,077 --> 01:05:42,147
Thank you.

1731
01:05:43,377 --> 01:05:45,217
I'm Cho Jung Seok, sir.

1732
01:05:45,217 --> 01:05:47,487
As much as I am Gummy's husband.

1733
01:05:47,687 --> 01:05:48,717
I wanted to tell you.

1734
01:05:48,717 --> 01:05:49,787
(Laughing)

1735
01:05:50,057 --> 01:05:51,287
- Hope your business flourishes.
- Thank you.

1736
01:05:51,287 --> 01:05:53,657
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1737
01:05:53,997 --> 01:05:56,127
- It's all seafood here.
- There's a lot of seafood.

1738
01:05:56,127 --> 01:05:57,167
(Now that we've eaten well, let's go grocery shopping.)

1739
01:05:57,797 --> 01:05:59,997
- Goodness.
- My gosh.

1740
01:05:59,997 --> 01:06:02,497
- It's big.
- Amazing.

1741
01:06:02,497 --> 01:06:05,337
(They buy a gigantic small octopus which will go into jjamppong.)

1742
01:06:05,437 --> 01:06:06,607
It looks good.

1743
01:06:06,607 --> 01:06:08,637
(They buy more than enough meat for tangsuyuk and japchae too.)

1744
01:06:09,077 --> 01:06:12,077
- Hello.
- Hello.

1745
01:06:12,707 --> 01:06:15,817
- Do you go to supermarkets often?
- Yes, I do.

1746
01:06:17,687 --> 01:06:18,747
It was a long day, wasn't it?

1747
01:06:19,247 --> 01:06:20,287
- Today?
- Yes.

1748
01:06:20,287 --> 01:06:22,487
- No, today wasn't bad. I had fun.
- Mudflat...

1749
01:06:23,257 --> 01:06:26,857
Is this supposed to follow a certain concept?

1750
01:06:27,397 --> 01:06:30,157
- Yes, we have a concept.
- Oh, you do.

1751
01:06:30,397 --> 01:06:32,067
- Today's concept is...
- Yes.

1752
01:06:32,067 --> 01:06:34,667
"Who is Cho Jung Seok? Who is he?"

1753
01:06:35,137 --> 01:06:36,567
- "Who is he?" - Yes.

1754
01:06:37,307 --> 01:06:38,367
I'm Gummy's husband.

1755
01:06:39,637 --> 01:06:40,677
Really?

1756
01:06:40,677 --> 01:06:42,807
I'm filming "Who is Cho Jong Seok?"

1757
01:06:42,807 --> 01:06:44,577
Excuse me, but I'm not Cho Jong Seok.

1758
01:06:45,407 --> 01:06:46,477
I'm Cho Jung Seok.

1759
01:06:46,607 --> 01:06:48,347
- It's my pronunciation issue.
- Last time...

1760
01:06:48,447 --> 01:06:50,247
Cho Jung Seok.

1761
01:06:50,247 --> 01:06:53,187
Cho Jong Seok.

1762
01:06:53,287 --> 01:06:54,357
Cho Jong Seok.

1763
01:06:54,457 --> 01:06:56,517
You have one lighting turned on...

1764
01:06:56,517 --> 01:06:59,027
under a dim light, right?

1765
01:06:59,027 --> 01:07:00,727
- It's one candle.
- Oh, candle.

1766
01:07:01,897 --> 01:07:03,997
You're terrible, producer.

