(What is this sound?)

2279
01:26:28,959 --> 01:26:30,919
(Chopping)

2280
01:26:31,459 --> 01:26:32,889
(Sun Young prepares the vegetables...)

2281
01:26:32,889 --> 01:26:34,359
(at an amazing speed this time.)

2282
01:26:34,789 --> 01:26:36,299
You can go slow, Sun Young.

2283
01:26:36,459 --> 01:26:37,759
That's something I can't do.

2284
01:26:38,929 --> 01:26:40,599
(She chops the vegetables at lightning speed...)

2285
01:26:40,599 --> 01:26:42,469
(as she is Wasp Sun Young.)

2286
01:26:42,739 --> 01:26:44,139
Gosh. You're good at chopping.

2287
01:26:44,139 --> 01:26:45,139
(Amazed)

2288
01:26:45,369 --> 01:26:46,409
(Chopping)

2289
01:26:46,409 --> 01:26:47,969
(The pleasant chopping sound spreads across the yard.)

2290
01:26:48,469 --> 01:26:52,149
Sun Young, you sound like Han Seok Bong's mother.

2291
01:26:53,209 --> 01:26:55,779
"You will rinse the clams..."

2292
01:26:56,479 --> 01:26:57,819
"while I chop the onions."

2293
01:26:58,589 --> 01:27:00,819
("Yes, Mother.")

2294
01:27:01,249 --> 01:27:03,759
(While the sisters are busy prepping the ingredients,)

2295
01:27:04,119 --> 01:27:08,359
(the brick stoves is almost ready too.)

2296
01:27:08,799 --> 01:27:10,759
(After placing the last 2 bricks,)

2297
01:27:11,199 --> 01:27:12,729
- It's perfect.
- Okay.

2298
01:27:13,069 --> 01:27:14,129
We did a good job.

2299
01:27:14,129 --> 01:27:15,199
(the sturdy stoves are ready...)

2300
01:27:15,199 --> 01:27:16,369
(to handle the siblings' dishes.)

2301
01:27:16,499 --> 01:27:18,399
We don't need to burn the firewood yet, right?

2302
01:27:18,609 --> 01:27:19,669
- No.
- Okay.

2303
01:27:20,039 --> 01:27:21,139
How can I help?

2304
01:27:22,579 --> 01:27:23,709
I'm making the crushed cucumber salad,

2305
01:27:23,709 --> 01:27:26,509
so you need to strike them, You Seok.

2306
01:27:28,549 --> 01:27:29,979
- Do I strike the cucumbers?
- Yes.

2307
01:27:31,119 --> 01:27:32,289
With my fist?

2308
01:27:32,889 --> 01:27:33,989
"With my fist?"

2309
01:27:34,119 --> 01:27:35,459
Why would you strike the cucumbers with your fist?

2310
01:27:35,459 --> 01:27:36,459
(Please spare the cucumbers.)

2311
01:27:36,819 --> 01:27:38,889
(What should I strike them with?)

2312
01:27:39,189 --> 01:27:40,529
- Now?
- No.

2313
01:27:40,529 --> 01:27:42,499
(First, she puts the cucumbers with trimmed ends in a bag.)

2314
01:27:42,759 --> 01:27:43,999
You know what the crushed cucumber salad looks like, right?

2315
01:27:43,999 --> 01:27:45,299
- I do.
- Okay.

2316
01:27:45,369 --> 01:27:47,129
I brought you a mallet.

2317
01:27:47,129 --> 01:27:48,899
(He needs to smash them with the mallet, not his fist.)

2318
01:27:49,299 --> 01:27:50,639
(You Seok tries smashing cucumbers for the first time.)

2319
01:27:50,639 --> 01:27:51,669
Goodness.

2320
01:27:52,839 --> 01:27:54,409
(He grabs the mallet.)

2321
01:27:54,539 --> 01:27:57,509
(He starts to beat the cucumbers.)

2322
01:27:57,909 --> 01:28:00,179
(Crushing)

2323
01:28:00,609 --> 01:28:03,249
(Joyful pounding)

2324
01:28:04,149 --> 01:28:06,149
(In Search of Taean's Sound)

2325
01:28:06,789 --> 01:28:08,689
(This is the sound made by Kang You Seok,)

2326
01:28:08,689 --> 01:28:11,019
(who lives in Sindu-ri, Taean-gun, South Chungcheong Province,)

2327
01:28:11,319 --> 01:28:15,159
(to make a smashed cucumber salad.)

2328
01:28:15,629 --> 01:28:18,299
(After smashing them hard a few more times,)

2329
01:28:18,399 --> 01:28:20,869
I smashed them this much.

2330
01:28:20,869 --> 01:28:21,899
(they are completely crushed.)

2331
01:28:22,239 --> 01:28:24,469
(He pours the well-smashed cucumber into a bowl.)

2332
01:28:24,939 --> 01:28:29,579
(It is seasoned with salt and sugar.)

2333
01:28:30,139 --> 01:28:33,549
(Jung Ah also adds a generous amount of vinegar to add the tang.)

2334
01:28:33,979 --> 01:28:36,449
(Lastly, she gives it a nice mix...)

2335
01:28:36,449 --> 01:28:38,919
(after adding minced garlic and sesame seeds.)

2336
01:28:39,389 --> 01:28:42,189
(Then sweet and sour smashed cucumber salad is done.)

2337
01:28:42,289 --> 01:28:43,559
- Here.
- Do you want to try it?

2338
01:28:44,059 --> 01:28:45,789
Will you tell me what I should add more?

2339
01:28:46,189 --> 01:28:47,229
I'd love to.

2340
01:28:47,229 --> 01:28:50,359
(Sun Young tastes it.)

2341
01:28:50,359 --> 01:28:52,069
- It's good.
- It's sweet and salty.

2342
01:28:52,869 --> 01:28:56,239
Jung Ah, please give me another piece.

2343
01:28:57,269 --> 01:28:58,769
(Putting another piece into her mouth)

2344
01:28:58,769 --> 01:28:59,969
- Yes.
- It's tasty.

2345
01:29:00,839 --> 01:29:02,239
I can't wait to eat it.

2346
01:29:02,239 --> 01:29:03,309
(Its refreshing kick whets her palate.)

2347
01:29:03,739 --> 01:29:05,479
(Next, it's time to make pepper japchae.)

2348
01:29:05,479 --> 01:29:06,949
(Smashed cucumber salad, pepper japchae, tangsuyuk, jjamppong)

2349
01:29:07,349 --> 01:29:12,449
(But they are still prepping the ingredients.)

2350
01:29:13,089 --> 01:29:15,819
(At that moment, Jung Seok suddenly goes to the room.)

2351
01:29:17,419 --> 01:29:19,489
(He grabs the acoustic guitar he saw earlier.)

2352
01:29:19,929 --> 01:29:22,659
(Then he comes back to the yard.)

2353
01:29:22,959 --> 01:29:24,099
Sing us a work song.

2354
01:29:24,229 --> 01:29:25,999
Yes. Sing us a song.

2355
01:29:27,329 --> 01:29:30,899
(A work song? Really?)

2356
01:29:31,399 --> 01:29:35,679
(What song will he sing for them?)

2357
01:29:36,109 --> 01:29:39,479
(Tuning)

2358
01:29:40,249 --> 01:29:42,379
How many chili peppers should I chop lengthwise, Jung Ah?

2359
01:29:42,679 --> 01:29:45,489
- How many should I chop?
- Lengthwise

2360
01:29:45,749 --> 01:29:46,849
He's singing.

2361
01:29:46,849 --> 01:29:48,719
(The performance starts without a warning.)

2362
01:29:49,359 --> 01:29:52,589
(Lengthwise, Jung Ah)

2363
01:29:52,589 --> 01:29:53,589
(Humming)

2364
01:29:54,729 --> 01:29:55,729
I love it.

2365
01:29:56,599 --> 01:29:57,659
He's singing.

2366
01:29:57,659 --> 01:29:59,599
(He's happy to watch him sing in the 1st row.)

2367
01:30:00,369 --> 01:30:01,529
(Singing)

2368
01:30:02,639 --> 01:30:03,899
(Singing)

2369
01:30:06,209 --> 01:30:08,669
(I want to eat it)

2370
01:30:08,979 --> 01:30:10,979
(The pepper japchae)

2371
01:30:12,909 --> 01:30:15,279
(Singing random stuff with his sweet voice)

2372
01:30:15,849 --> 01:30:19,349
(I want to eat it)

2373
01:30:19,349 --> 01:30:21,189
(Based on the lyrics,)

2374
01:30:21,189 --> 01:30:25,489
(he must be dying to have some pepper japchae.)

2375
01:30:26,059 --> 01:30:30,629
(Still, they get immersed in his song.)

2376
01:30:31,099 --> 01:30:34,069
Gosh. Look at him. He's amazing.

2377
01:30:34,069 --> 01:30:35,099
(There are his fans everywhere.)

2378
01:30:35,599 --> 01:30:37,099
(Thank you)

2379
01:30:38,739 --> 01:30:40,209
(For telling me)

2380
01:30:41,109 --> 01:30:42,539
- He's really good.
- That I'm amazing

2381
01:30:42,539 --> 01:30:43,609
Go away.

2382
01:30:44,639 --> 01:30:45,779
(That's it.)

2383
01:30:45,949 --> 01:30:47,149
That was crazy.

2384
01:30:47,149 --> 01:30:48,579
(His stunning voice captivated the female fans' hearts.)

2385
01:30:48,579 --> 01:30:50,019
- Cho Jung Seok.
- Encore.

2386
01:30:50,019 --> 01:30:51,419
- Cho Jung Seok.
- Encore.

2387
01:30:51,919 --> 01:30:53,919
(Let's change the mood this time.)

2388
01:30:54,119 --> 01:30:55,119
(Singing)

2389
01:30:55,119 --> 01:30:56,189
That's great.

2390
01:30:56,319 --> 01:30:58,089
What did you do with the chilis after washing them?

2391
01:30:58,089 --> 01:31:00,829
What did you do with the washed chili peppers?

2392
01:31:00,829 --> 01:31:03,529
(Having a culture shock)

2393
01:31:04,199 --> 01:31:07,599
What do we do with the chilis after washing them?

2394
01:31:07,599 --> 01:31:08,629
Did you drain them?

2395
01:31:08,799 --> 01:31:09,839
What do we do?

2396
01:31:09,839 --> 01:31:11,239
(There they are)

2397
01:31:11,239 --> 01:31:12,639
(Please tell me)

2398
01:31:12,639 --> 01:31:14,009
(Singing)

2399
01:31:16,079 --> 01:31:17,909
I want to know

2400
01:31:17,909 --> 01:31:19,409
(They're over here)

2401
01:31:19,409 --> 01:31:21,209
(Both Manila clams and chili peppers are in rock spirit.)

2402
01:31:21,749 --> 01:31:22,749
(Falling for Jung Seok)

2403
01:31:22,749 --> 01:31:25,319
He's good. It's nice to play the guitar well.

2404
01:31:28,819 --> 01:31:30,689
(Singing)

2405
01:31:30,689 --> 01:31:31,989
(Highest audience satisfaction rate)

2406
01:31:31,989 --> 01:31:34,289
He's amazing.

2407
01:31:34,759 --> 01:31:36,559
(He's suddenly embarrassed when he's done singing.)

2408
01:31:36,559 --> 01:31:37,929
- Sorry.
- I love the metal.

2409
01:31:39,129 --> 01:31:40,229
It's so nice...

2410
01:31:40,329 --> 01:31:43,169
to have live music when cooking.

2411
01:31:43,669 --> 01:31:45,569
- Are we done prepping?
- Yes, we are.

2412
01:31:45,569 --> 01:31:46,669
(Prepping is done. Meat, onions, shiitake and button mushrooms,)

2413
01:31:46,669 --> 01:31:47,769
(Cheongyang chili pepper, julienned bamboo shoots)

2414
01:31:48,209 --> 01:31:50,639
- I'll start the fire, then.
- Okay.

2415
01:31:50,639 --> 01:31:53,049
- Okay.
- Should I do it, Jung Seok?

2416
01:31:53,049 --> 01:31:55,109
No. I'm a Warrior of Fire.

2417
01:31:55,479 --> 01:31:56,519
Really?

2418
01:31:57,219 --> 01:31:58,779
(How to start a fire by the Warrior of Fire)

2419
01:31:58,779 --> 01:32:00,389
(Get lots of dried firewood first.)

2420
01:32:01,019 --> 01:32:04,359
(Stack them in a crisscross pattern for the air to go through.)

2421
01:32:04,859 --> 01:32:07,529
(After stacking the firewood,)

2422
01:32:08,689 --> 01:32:12,899
(why don't we get the fire roaring?)

2423
01:32:13,369 --> 01:32:15,999
(Skillfully fan the fire to supply it with air.)

2424
01:32:17,639 --> 01:32:18,769
(Blazing)

2425
01:32:19,509 --> 01:32:22,009
(The fire blazes in no time.)

2426
01:32:22,939 --> 01:32:25,849
It's done. It's lit.

2427
01:32:26,279 --> 01:32:27,709
Gosh. I was back in my element after a while.

2428
01:32:27,709 --> 01:32:28,809
(He's the Warrior of Fire, indeed.)

2429
01:32:29,249 --> 01:32:31,719
You're good at starting a fire too, Jung Seok.

2430
01:32:32,689 --> 01:32:34,119
- Hold on.
- I just need to...

2431
01:32:34,119 --> 01:32:35,149
(But...)

2432
01:32:36,119 --> 01:32:37,759
- The flames are really strong.
- They are strong.

2433
01:32:37,759 --> 01:32:39,689
(It's way too strong.)

2434
01:32:40,289 --> 01:32:42,399
I always do this because I'm the Warrior of Fire.

2435
01:32:42,399 --> 01:32:43,429
(I'm so the Warrior of Fire.)

2436
01:32:43,699 --> 01:32:45,899
(He's funny.)

2437
01:32:46,329 --> 01:32:47,499
Can you turn it down?

2438
01:32:47,499 --> 01:32:48,899
(By the way, can you lower the heat?)

2439
01:32:49,169 --> 01:32:51,369
Of course, I can. Do you want medium heat?

2440
01:32:51,369 --> 01:32:53,109
- Yes. Medium heat, please.
- Medium heat? Okay.

2441
01:32:53,969 --> 01:32:56,239
(The Warrior can do anything, including the heat control.)

2442
01:32:56,239 --> 01:32:57,309
I'll take some out.

2443
01:32:58,709 --> 01:32:59,709
(Subdued)

2444
01:32:59,709 --> 01:33:00,779
The heat is lowered.

2445
01:33:01,679 --> 01:33:02,749
- This will be good.
- It's great.

2446
01:33:02,749 --> 01:33:04,619
- Good. Place the wok.
- Okay.

2447
01:33:05,319 --> 01:33:06,519
What are you cooking here?

2448
01:33:06,519 --> 01:33:08,819
- She'll stir-fry... Pepper japchae.
- Pepper Japchae.

2449
01:33:09,589 --> 01:33:12,829
(Adding a generous amount of oil into the heated pan)

2450
01:33:13,029 --> 01:33:15,229
- It's still hot.
- It's okay.

2451
01:33:15,229 --> 01:33:16,299
(Amid the intense heat...)

2452
01:33:16,299 --> 01:33:17,859
This one? Which one should I give you?

2453
01:33:17,859 --> 01:33:20,769
(appears a woman.)

2454
01:33:21,269 --> 01:33:23,969
(Adding more oil)

2455
01:33:24,469 --> 01:33:27,539
(Pouring the pre-seasoned pork)

2456
01:33:28,039 --> 01:33:32,179
(She starts stir-frying it joyfully.)

2457
01:33:32,579 --> 01:33:34,309
Is there too much pork? It doesn't cook well.

2458
01:33:35,779 --> 01:33:37,449
If you want me...

2459
01:33:37,919 --> 01:33:40,219
to increase the heat, I can do that.

2460
01:33:41,249 --> 01:33:42,289
Should I turn up the heat? Okay.

2461
01:33:42,289 --> 01:33:44,519
(The mysterious woman wants a stronger fire.)

2462
01:33:44,819 --> 01:33:46,459
- The heat is good now.
- Okay.

2463
01:33:46,459 --> 01:33:47,489
(The hot fire can't stop...)

2464
01:33:47,959 --> 01:33:49,899
(this master of the smoky flavors.)

2465
01:33:50,859 --> 01:33:52,129
It has to be fully cooked.

2466
01:33:52,129 --> 01:33:54,329
(Deity Yum of Chinese Cuisine)

2467
01:33:54,869 --> 01:33:57,569
(Chinese cuisine is all about smoky flavors.)

2468
01:33:57,569 --> 01:34:00,239
(Stir-frying the meat quickly as if charring it over high heat)

2469
01:34:00,839 --> 01:34:02,879
(Not holding back on the spicy chili oil)

2470
01:34:02,879 --> 01:34:05,009
(Squeezing)

2471
01:34:05,539 --> 01:34:07,379
(After adding the julienned bell pepper,)

2472
01:34:07,379 --> 01:34:09,619
(mushrooms, onions, chilis, and bamboo shoots,)

2473
01:34:09,919 --> 01:34:13,549
(she stir-fries them mercilessly.)

2474
01:34:14,119 --> 01:34:17,389
(Blazing)

2475
01:34:17,759 --> 01:34:21,989
(This is how to add the smoky flavor.)

2476
01:34:22,799 --> 01:34:23,859
Gosh. Look at the fire.

2477
01:34:23,859 --> 01:34:24,899
(After adding the smoky flavor,)

2478
01:34:26,669 --> 01:34:28,699
(she adds the chili oil for the 2nd time.)

2479
01:34:29,769 --> 01:34:34,809
(A strong spiciness is added to the smoky flavor.)

2480
01:34:35,269 --> 01:34:36,839
Will you add a bit more chili oil?

2481
01:34:36,839 --> 01:34:39,249
(It's not over yet.)

2482
01:34:40,109 --> 01:34:41,149
- A swirl of it?
- Yes.

2483
01:34:42,249 --> 01:34:43,249
Drizzle it.

2484
01:34:43,949 --> 01:34:45,019
Good.

2485
01:34:46,449 --> 01:34:48,719
(Cheongyang chili peppers, chili oil, and smoky flavor)

2486
01:34:48,719 --> 01:34:51,059
(Unfathomable spiciness)

2487
01:34:51,389 --> 01:34:53,959
- Gosh. It looks so good.
- It looks really good.

2488
01:34:53,959 --> 01:34:55,829
(People are drooling.)

2489
01:34:56,359 --> 01:34:58,099
(Adding umami with the soy sauce and oyster sauce)

2490
01:34:58,099 --> 01:34:59,129
It's the oyster sauce.

2491
01:34:59,869 --> 01:35:03,099
(For the finishing touch, she adds the black pepper.)

2492
01:35:03,539 --> 01:35:04,799
It's hot. I'll do it.

2493
01:35:06,439 --> 01:35:08,009
(You Seok takes over...)

2494
01:35:08,009 --> 01:35:10,209
(since it must be hot for Jung Ah to be near the fire.)

2495
01:35:10,739 --> 01:35:12,979
(She's proud of him.)

2496
01:35:13,449 --> 01:35:16,319
(Doing his best)

2497
01:35:16,549 --> 01:35:17,979
Stir-fry them...

2498
01:35:17,979 --> 01:35:19,419
- until the vegetables are soft.
- Okay.

2499
01:35:19,419 --> 01:35:21,389
(After stir-frying them until the vegetables are soft,)

2500
01:35:21,819 --> 01:35:24,989
(he coats it with the smoky flavor.)

2501
01:35:26,259 --> 01:35:28,429
(Then spicy pepper japchae is ready.)

2502
01:35:28,429 --> 01:35:29,499
Is the pepper japchae finished?

2503
01:35:29,499 --> 01:35:32,999
(Then spicy pepper japchae is ready.)

2504
01:35:33,369 --> 01:35:35,099
- Jung Seok.
- Yes? You try it first.

2505
01:35:35,099 --> 01:35:36,099
No.

2506
01:35:36,439 --> 01:35:37,499
(Putting in his mouth)

2507
01:35:38,939 --> 01:35:40,909
(How is it, Jung Seok?)

2508
01:35:41,809 --> 01:35:43,179
Gosh. It's good.

2509
01:35:43,939 --> 01:35:45,009
It's tasty.

2510
01:35:46,049 --> 01:35:50,049
(Sun Young tries a bite too.)

2511
01:35:55,789 --> 01:35:56,989
(It's really tasty, Jung Ah.)

2512
01:35:56,989 --> 01:35:59,329
- It's good, isn't it?
- It's sweet. It's crazy.

2513
01:35:59,329 --> 01:36:00,329
(Shocked)

2514
01:36:00,329 --> 01:36:01,359
How could you do it?

2515
01:36:02,129 --> 01:36:03,159
It's so good, Jung Ah.

2516
01:36:03,159 --> 01:36:05,499
(It's totally delicious.)

2517
01:36:05,499 --> 01:36:06,569
(Amazed)

2518
01:36:07,499 --> 01:36:08,899
- It's better than restaurants.
- Exactly.

2519
01:36:08,899 --> 01:36:10,099
- Gosh. Seriously.
- It tastes really good.

2520
01:36:11,169 --> 01:36:12,609
- Do you have chopsticks?
- Yes.

2521
01:36:12,609 --> 01:36:13,669
(She gives some to the production staff to taste.)

2522
01:36:14,039 --> 01:36:15,639
(It's so good.)

2523
01:36:16,239 --> 01:36:18,579
What tastes good? Is the crushed cucumber salad good too?

2524
01:36:19,179 --> 01:36:21,149
When you taste the pepper japchae,

2525
01:36:21,149 --> 01:36:23,049
- it'll blow your mind.
- It's tasty right now.

2526
01:36:23,819 --> 01:36:24,819
That's done.

2527
01:36:24,819 --> 01:36:25,849
